{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,280p' 'Pipeline/ArchitectureReview/outputs/codex/runs/20260823T102213Z-35a76864/reviews/game_technical_director.json'\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"agent\": \"Pragmatic Game Technical Director\",\n  \"provider\": \"openai-codex\",\n  \"model\": \"gpt-5.6-sol\",\n  \"reasoning_effort\": \"high\",\n  \"duration_seconds\": 459.15,\n  \"agent_runtime_run_id\": \"game-technical-director-26e550e3c64c4ff9\",\n  \"agent_runtime_artifacts\": \"Pipeline/ArchitectureReview/outputs/codex/runs/20260823T102213Z-35a76864/agent_runtime/game-technical-director-26e550e3c64c4ff9\",\n  \"result\": {\n    \"alternative_architecture\": {\n      \"description\": \"Replace the milestone stack with a thin delivery-first loop. State: keep the GDD, Git main, and small versioned contracts only for active/near-term slices; derive operational status from persisted run state, Git/PR state, and validation manifests. Planning: a human selects the next vertical slice and approves its behavior; an LLM produces a bounded contract plus GDD-section impact map. Execution: a local driver creates one branch/worktree and invokes one write-capable worker, followed by a fresh reviewer. Validation: run deterministic checks and Unity compile/EditMode/PlayMode tests through the clean runner, then require human checks for feel and visuals. Recovery: persist a small state machine—planned, implementing, validating, needs-repair, needs-human, merged—with commits, evidence paths, and bounded retry counts. GDD changes: map changed sections or stable requirement IDs only to affected contracts, classifying them as unaffected, contract-review, revalidation, or rework; never globally rebuild the backlog by default. Unity integration: the Windows Unity host owns engine execution, outputs XML/logs outside the repository, checks tree cleanliness, and distinguishes in-memory builders from committed scene/prefab conformance.\",\n      \"needed\": true,\n      \"why_better\": \"It retains the safety mechanisms supported by actual failures while making gameplay delivery the primary proof. It eliminates several authority handoffs, handles an iterative GDD causally instead of through a whole-document hash, and can produce useful game progress before scheduling, artifact generation, or parallelism exist.\"\n    },\n    \"architecture_summary\": \"The repository contains four substantial production foundations: a 37-contract TaskGraph, validated GDD retrieval, evidence-derived conformance, and provider-neutral read/review invocation. It does not contain the production path that creates throughput: no enabled readiness, dispatch authorization, write-capable gameplay worker, execution crew, Git lifecycle, Unity execution, merge loop, or completion propagation. The result is a sophisticated safety and audit shell around a small Unity prototype, not yet an autonomous game-development system.\",\n    \"biggest_uncertainty\": \"The frozen repository cannot show whether a separate development machine can execute reliable automated Unity runs for new work. It records credible prior Unity 6000.1.8f1 results, but no new production task has traversed the proposed end-to-end loop.\",\n    \"confidence\": 0.94,\n    \"do_not_build_yet\": [\n      \"Continuous scheduling and backlog replenishment\",\n      \"Parallel workers, generalized leases, and resource-lock scheduling\",\n      \"GitHub Issues/Projects synchronization\",\n      \"Automatic merge or provider fallback\",\n      \"The bundled Progressive Decomposer platform\",\n      \"Artifact Authority and Artifact GER until a real design artifact blocks delivery\",\n      \"More provider adapters or ArchitectureReview plumbing\",\n      \"Top-k-only context packs presented as complete canon\"\n    ],\n    \"evidence\": [\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"Successful read-only diagnostics at the frozen commit reported 37 valid schema-v2 contracts, an acyclic graph, disabled autonomous dispatch, unavailable readiness, zero authorized tasks, and a clean working tree before and after.\",\n        \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"NSC-023 derives as conformant from its committed baseline, demonstrating that the evidence evaluator works for one historical feature.\",\n        \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskGraph/evidence/NSC-023/records/BASE-NSC-023-86af98f41ab5.json\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"The production GDD index validated as CURRENT with 41 chunks and matching source hash, but documentation says the whole GDD must still be supplied because retrieval coverage is unproven.\",\n        \"path\": \"Pipeline/GDDRAG\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"AgentRuntime explicitly lacks repository writing, approved command execution, gameplay roles, Unity, GER, task selection, Git workflow, readiness, and authorization.\",\n        \"path\": \"Pipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"TaskExecution is currently only an immutable task-identity wrapper around one generic invocation.\",\n        \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskExecution/task_runner.py\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"NSC-003 declares itself concrete and single-agent, while current-state guidance identifies unresolved input arbitration, steering, cancellation, arrival, pathing, and restriction semantics.\",\n        \"path\": \"Tasks/NSC-003.yaml\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"The GDD still names Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity as canonical, while implementation and evidence moved authority to Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity.\",\n        \"path\": \"Docs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"The conformance evaluator compares every evidence record against the hash of the entire current GDD, so any GDD text change makes otherwise unchanged evidence stale.\",\n        \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskGraph/current_conformance.py\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"The camera GER passed static review twice while remaining unusable in Unity, then encountered a no-op refinement before succeeding through runtime feedback and bounded retries.\",\n        \"path\": \"Assignment6GER/README_Assignment6.md\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"Earlier builder tests called the production scene-saving entry point; later commits added an in-memory seam, direct committed-scene tests, and byte-preservation checks.\",\n        \"path\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"The actual project still has direct hardware polling for WASD and door interaction, no spells or enemy runtime, missing required navigation packages, and no registered build scene.\",\n        \"path\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"Across the 244 commits after the camera feature commit, 136 touched Pipeline, only three touched Assets/NoSafeCircle, and none touched runtime gameplay scripts; those three game-area changes were scene/test safety work rather than a new mechanic.\",\n        \"path\": \"Git history: 20c5228..9f2485d\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"Pipeline areas contain roughly 13,000 nonblank lines across TaskGraph, GDDRAG, AgentRuntime, and TaskExecution, versus roughly 1,448 under Assets/NoSafeCircle; Reconciliation adds about 84,000 nonblank lines including generated history.\",\n        \"path\": \"Pipeline/\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"CURRENT_STATE contains contradictory lifecycle claims: its opening describes Stage 4C/Codex migration as implemented, while its later Immediate Next Goal says Claude migration is next and Codex remains unimplemented.\",\n        \"path\": \"Docs/AI-Pipeline/CURRENT_STATE.md\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"gdd_iteration_concerns\": [\n      \"The present whole-GDD hash treats an unrelated wording, art, balance, or repository-description edit as grounds to revalidate every delivered task.\",\n      \"Contracts copy substantial GDD prose and bootstrap repository observations, creating a second version of design/current-state facts that can drift independently.\",\n      \"Stable requirement IDs and an implemented requirement-to-task impact map do not exist.\",\n      \"The promised reconciliation-to-graph diff/review/apply path is not implemented, so immutable snapshots do not synchronize the living graph.\",\n      \"The scene relocation demonstrates the problem now: canon, contract bootstrap evidence, current implementation, and conformance evidence disagree on the canonical path while NSC-023 still derives as conformant.\",\n      \"When canon changes, the correct flow should be scoped impact review: identify affected requirements, amend or supersede only affected contracts, decide revalidation versus rework, preserve prior delivery evidence as lineage, and deterministically recalculate affected dependencies.\",\n      \"Full reconciliation should be reserved for major scope changes, milestone audits, or evidence that the graph has materially diverged—not normal iterative GDD editing.\"\n    ],\n    \"human_intervention_points\": [\n      \"Approve gameplay semantics where the GDD leaves feel, arbitration, cancellation, navigation, or tuning ambiguous.\",\n      \"Play the game to judge movement feel, camera framing, readability, animation, encounter pacing, balance, and fun.\",\n      \"Inspect scene, prefab, package, Input Actions, and build-configuration changes before merge.\",\n      \"Resolve architectural changes and cross-system ownership conflicts discovered during implementation.\",\n      \"Approve canon amendments, contract supersession, and generated design/content.\",\n      \"Review and merge changes until the single-ticket lane has a strong production track record.\",\n      \"Perform final Windows build, device/input, performance, and presentation validation.\"\n    ],\n    \"hypothetical_failure_solutions\": [\n      \"Parallel resource locks and generalized claims protect against multi-worker conflicts before one production worker exists.\",\n      \"GitHub dashboard synchronization addresses visibility at a scale the project has not reached.\",\n      \"Automatic provider fallback protects availability but risks changing behavior and is not an observed delivery blocker.\",\n      \"Artifact Authority, artifact promotion, and multi-evaluator Artifact GER address future generated-design work; the current bootstrap contains zero artifact tasks.\",\n      \"Continuous scheduling, backlog replenishment, merge queues, and daily budget governance protect later unattended scale.\",\n      \"Most adversarial immutable-evidence ancestry and ambiguity cases are prudent hardening but have not materially accelerated the one existing production baseline.\",\n      \"Top-k context optimization addresses future token cost, while the current policy still sends the entire relatively small GDD.\"\n    ],\n    \"missing_components\": [\n      \"An approved dependency-readiness rule derived from current conformance\",\n      \"A write-capable, scope-bounded implementation invocation\",\n      \"A minimal branch/worktree execution driver\",\n      \"Task-specific Unity compile, EditMode, PlayMode, and committed-artifact validation\",\n      \"A small persisted recovery state machine around one delivery attempt\",\n      \"A deterministic diff between evolving canon, task contracts, and delivered surfaces\",\n      \"A reviewed mechanism for amending or superseding affected contracts\",\n      \"A proven context builder that cannot omit cross-cutting canon\",\n      \"Actual gameplay integration through review, merge, evidence publication, and downstream readiness\"\n    ],\n    \"next_slice\": {\n      \"deliverables\": [\n        \"A short human-approved decision note resolving primary click, held-pointer steering, UI click suppression, command replacement/cancellation, arrival behavior, and prototype pathing expectations\",\n        \"Input Actions-backed pointer position and primary-click actions\",\n        \"PlayerMovement-owned world-space pointer projection and destination/hold steering\",\n        \"Owner-controlled movement restriction, suspend/re-enable, and restart interfaces\",\n        \"Integration with door selection so one click can request approach without independent pointer projection\",\n        \"Focused component and Play Mode tests using non-saving seams\",\n        \"A clean-tree Unity validation run with external XML/logs\",\n        \"Human Play Mode approval for movement feel, camera framing, UI arbitration, and door approach\",\n        \"One reviewed merge plus minimal delivery manifest sufficient to derive task conformance and unlock dependencies\"\n      ],\n      \"proof_of_value\": \"Starting from one approved contract, a bounded worker creates a gameplay diff, survives deterministic and Unity validation, incorporates runtime feedback through at most a small fixed repair budget, receives human feel approval, merges, and causes dependent work to become ready. That is the first credible demonstration of days-versus-weeks leverage.\",\n      \"title\": \"Playable mouse movement and door-approach delivery lane\",\n      \"why\": \"Movement is foundational to spells, doors, pursuit, restart, and victory suspension. It also exercises every currently unproven production boundary: design clarification, Input Actions, write execution, canonical-scene integration, runtime validation, repair, merge, conformance, and dependency propagation. Build only the narrow glue needed for this slice.\"\n    },\n    \"observed_failure_solutions\": [\n      \"Repository-backed state prevents loss of context between model sessions.\",\n      \"Bounded contracts reduced scope drift in the door, mana, and camera coursework runs.\",\n      \"Runtime evidence re-entering GER fixed camera defects that semantic/static review approved incorrectly.\",\n      \"No-op change detection prevented a refiner from claiming progress without modifying gameplay files.\",\n      \"Circuit breakers bounded repeated camera repair.\",\n      \"The Unity testing policy, clean runner, in-memory builder seam, and committed-scene checks directly address tests that previously saved canonical assets.\",\n      \"Scene identity/location checks address duplicate or ambiguous DoorPrototype scene authority.\",\n      \"Immutable reconciliation outputs and resume utilities address real reconciliation timeout, recovery, identity, and merge-conflict problems—although those are pipeline-self-management wins rather than game throughput.\",\n      \"Current production GDDRAG addresses the observed staleness of the older July Assignment 4 index.\",\n      \"Line-ending normalization addresses the repository's Windows/Linux validation boundary.\"\n    ],\n    \"overall_verdict\": \"partially_unsound\",\n    \"overengineering\": [\n      \"A multi-model, domain-parallel reconciliation and verification system was built before one production gameplay ticket could execute.\",\n      \"The one-time 37-contract bootstrap required extensive schema, refinement, recovery, finding-identity, and arbitration machinery disproportionate to this small game.\",\n      \"TaskGraph completion was replaced by a task-specific immutable evidence/conformance system before replacement readiness shipped, leaving the graph inert.\",\n      \"AgentRuntime has extensive hostile-value, schema, path, transport, and publication hardening while its providers remain incapable of implementing gameplay.\",\n      \"ArchitectureReview was chosen as the first production runtime consumer, proving review transport rather than game delivery.\",\n      \"Task contract, evidence record, conformance result, readiness, authorization, runtime request, task-execution request, reconciliation snapshot, and future GitHub state create too many handoffs for a single-developer capstone.\",\n      \"Large generated reconciliation history is stored in the source repository even though only the approved current contract delta is needed for day-to-day development.\",\n      \"Milestone plans include artifact generation, supervisor, continuous autonomy, and parallelism before a single corrected delivery path exists.\"\n    ],\n    \"state_and_authority_concerns\": [\n      \"Necessary authorities are: approved GDD/design decisions for intent; task contract for bounded scope; integrated Git tree for implementation; deterministic/Unity/human validation for acceptance; and human merge/canon approval.\",\n      \"It is useful to distinguish a provider claim from test evidence and current conformance from dispatch permission, but those distinctions do not each require a heavyweight independent subsystem.\",\n      \"Reconciliation snapshots are valid audit history, but they duplicate responsibility when treated as a standing operational layer alongside Tasks and current conformance.\",\n      \"Task contracts should not retain mutable repository-state observations as if they remain current facts.\",\n      \"AgentRuntime versus TaskExecution is a reasonable generic/task-specific boundary, but it currently adds audit ceremony without an execution consumer.\",\n      \"Operational run state should live in one restartable supervisor record or PR/check state, not be recreated across task files, evidence records, runtime artifacts, future GitHub fields, and status documents.\",\n      \"Git commit/PR identity plus a compact validation manifest can replace much of the bespoke evidence DAG for ordinary tasks; richer lineage is warranted only for revalidation or regulated/high-risk surfaces.\",\n      \"Human authority is currently correctly retained, but fail-closed authorization has become a permanent stop rather than a guard around an enabled narrow path.\"\n    ],\n    \"strong_decisions\": [\n      \"A deterministic local process—not an LLM context—should own continuity, budgets, retries, and recovery.\",\n      \"Workers should receive one bounded task and should not reconstruct the global roadmap.\",\n      \"Git and Unity evidence must outrank worker claims.\",\n      \"Implementation should be isolated from main, and merged/integrated state should define delivery.\",\n      \"Runtime, visual, and interaction evidence must be able to overturn static approval.\",\n      \"Canonical Unity scenes and prefabs must not be mutated by normal tests.\",\n      \"Missing design should be escalated rather than silently invented.\",\n      \"No-op repairs must consume retry budget.\",\n      \"Start with one worker; add parallelism only after reliable delivery.\",\n      \"Reconciliation should propose reviewed changes rather than directly rewriting operational state.\",\n      \"Design completeness and execution size are legitimately different questions.\",\n      \"Provider-neutral generic invocation is useful when kept below game-specific task semantics.\"\n    ],\n    \"structural_flaws\": [\n      \"The implemented architecture ends before the activities that produce game value: selecting, authorizing, writing, validating in Unity, merging, and unlocking dependent work.\",\n      \"Schema-v2 removed task completion status and deliberately disabled readiness before evidence-based dependency readiness was implemented.\",\n      \"The moving-GDD model is global and hash-based rather than scoped and causal.\",\n      \"The bootstrap classified NSC-003 as concrete/single-agent even though the repository's own current-state document now requires multiple human design decisions before implementation.\",\n      \"Conformance verifies record consistency and selected surfaces, not the semantic truth of every repository observation copied into a contract or GDD.\",\n      \"Documentation is not a reliable current-state control plane because the same file contains incompatible next-step and implementation claims.\",\n      \"The architecture plans a generic scanner, context builder, decomposer, artifact authority, supervisor, and execution crew as separate milestones instead of proving the smallest vertical delivery path.\",\n      \"The provider boundary assumes externally enforced read-only containment for repository review; no equivalent approved containment/write policy exists for gameplay implementation.\",\n      \"The current canonical scene is still a generated monolithic integration surface, so many nominally independent tasks will contend on the builder and scene until prefab/runtime composition boundaries improve.\",\n      \"The project has optimized correctness metadata while the required game remains at door/mana/camera prototype maturity with no spells, enemies, navigation foundation, restart, victory, or build scene registration.\"\n    ],\n    \"throughput_assessment\": \"Major near-term leverage is not currently plausible. The simpler historical crews did produce a door prototype, mana system, and camera feature, showing that bounded AI implementation can help. The production rewrite has not reproduced that result. Since the camera feature, the frozen ancestry contains 244 commits, 136 touching Pipeline, three touching the game area, and zero touching runtime gameplay scripts. Today the machinery can validate its graph, retrieve canon, inspect one conformance baseline, and run bounded read-only reviews; it cannot advance a gameplay task. If forbidden to build infrastructure for one slice, the first failure is immediate: taskcontrol cannot select work, authorization is denied, and AgentRuntime cannot write or run Unity. Progress would require manually bypassing the production machinery and using a human-driven coding/Unity workflow.\",\n    \"verdict_reason\": \"The architecture's governing principles are sound and worth retaining, but its production partitioning, milestone order, and GDD synchronization model are not. Safety infrastructure has displaced game development, the operational graph was made inert, and evolving canon is handled with coarse invalidation rather than reviewed impact. Reorganize around one thin write-test-review-merge gameplay lane; only add infrastructure when that lane exposes a repeated bottleneck.\"\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,280p' 'Pipeline/ArchitectureReview/outputs/codex/runs/20260823T102213Z-35a76864/reviews/game_producer.json'\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"agent\": \"Game Producer and Throughput Reviewer\",\n  \"provider\": \"openai-codex\",\n  \"model\": \"gpt-5.6-sol\",\n  \"reasoning_effort\": \"high\",\n  \"duration_seconds\": 558.58,\n  \"agent_runtime_run_id\": \"game-producer-12f432a4072247d9\",\n  \"agent_runtime_artifacts\": \"Pipeline/ArchitectureReview/outputs/codex/runs/20260823T102213Z-35a76864/agent_runtime/game-producer-12f432a4072247d9\",\n  \"result\": {\n    \"alternative_architecture\": {\n      \"description\": \"Reorganize around a thin, change-driven delivery controller. State: keep approved GDD requirements and immutable task-contract revisions in Git; keep one operational lifecycle ledger for planned/running/validating/blocked/review/done; treat the merge commit plus evidence manifest as delivery truth. Planning: human-prioritize one vertical slice and link it to stable requirement IDs; GDD diffs impact only linked work. Execution: one scoped writable coding worker on a branch, with checkpoint commits. Validation: deterministic Git checks, a real Windows Unity compile/EditMode/PlayMode/build adapter, one semantic diff review, and explicit human visual/feel gates. Recovery: reconcile attempt IDs against branches, commits, Unity artifacts, and merges so retries are idempotent. Unity integration: maintain one validated canonical scene registry and enforce project-lock/import-cache policy. Keep the existing GDDRAG, clean Unity runner, bounded runtime, and evidence concepts; demote global reconciliation to occasional audits.\",\n      \"needed\": true,\n      \"why_better\": \"It preserves the sound safety components while putting the missing delivery transaction at the center. It also treats GDD evolution as scoped change impact rather than globally invalidating evidence or rebuilding the roadmap.\"\n    },\n    \"architecture_summary\": \"The underlying principles are sound—bounded workers, deterministic facts, Git integration truth, runtime evidence, and human design authority—but the implemented architecture is not yet sound as an autonomous game-development investment. It is a heavily hardened read/review and evidence framework surrounding a nonexistent gameplay delivery loop. Worse, evolving-canon synchronization already fails: the canonical scene moved, yet the GDD, task contracts, and resource records still reference the deleted path while graph validation passes.\",\n    \"biggest_uncertainty\": \"The repository cannot reveal undocumented Unity-host automation or human workflows outside Git. If a reliable external execution/build lane already exists, the delivery gap is smaller, but it is not integrated with this architecture.\",\n    \"confidence\": 0.94,\n    \"do_not_build_yet\": [\n      \"A general continuous supervisor or automatic dispatcher.\",\n      \"Parallel workers, claims, merge queues, and broad worktree scheduling.\",\n      \"Bidirectional GitHub Issues/Projects synchronization; choose one operational authority first.\",\n      \"Progressive Decomposer and Artifact Authority/Artifact GER until a real feature is blocked by missing approved design.\",\n      \"Provider fallback or additional provider/reviewer migrations.\",\n      \"Another global reconciliation or multi-model verification cycle for ordinary GDD edits.\",\n      \"Top-k-only compact task context; the current GDD is small enough to provide in full.\",\n      \"More conformance-schema hardening before a new gameplay delivery exercises the existing model.\"\n    ],\n    \"evidence\": [\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"At the frozen commit, taskcontrol validation passes, but readiness is explicitly unavailable and authorization denies every task.\",\n        \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py:202\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"The conformance evaluator compares every record with a hash of the entire canonical GDD; any GDD edit makes otherwise unchanged evidence stale.\",\n        \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskGraph/current_conformance.py:164\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"OpenAI/Codex rejects repository writing and approved command execution, so the implemented provider path cannot advance gameplay.\",\n        \"path\": \"Pipeline/AgentRuntime/providers/openai_codex.py:89\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"TaskExecution only publishes task_request.json and delegates one generic invocation; it has no planning, Git, Unity, GER, evidence-publication, or completion behavior.\",\n        \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskExecution/task_runner.py\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"The authoritative scene is now Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity, but numerous task contracts and resource locks still reference the deleted Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity.\",\n        \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskGraph/RESOURCE_GROUPS.yaml:108\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"NSC-037 still says the current authoritative scene is the deleted path and incorrectly classifies the actual authoritative scene as a non-canonical stub.\",\n        \"path\": \"Tasks/NSC-037.yaml\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"The current GDD itself still declares the deleted scene path canonical, demonstrating that a hash-current RAG can faithfully serve stale canon relative to implementation.\",\n        \"path\": \"Docs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md:269\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"The Windows build has no registered scenes.\",\n        \"path\": \"ProjectSettings/EditorBuildSettings.asset:7\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"Current gameplay movement still directly polls WASD and does not use the planned mouse-directed Input Actions path.\",\n        \"path\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts/PlayerMovement.cs:22\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"Assignment 6 records two static-evaluator passes that remained unusable in Unity, followed by runtime-driven repairs and a no-op refinement rejection.\",\n        \"path\": \"Assignment6GER/README_Assignment6.md\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"The clean Unity runner was created after a passing builder test destructively rewrote a tracked canonical scene.\",\n        \"path\": \"Pipeline/Testing/README.md\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"On the current HEAD ancestry after Assignment 6, 244 commits added about 115,877 lines under Pipeline/Docs/Tasks, while only three commits touched Assets/Packages/ProjectSettings—and those addressed test safety and scene relocation, not a new gameplay feature.\",\n        \"path\": \"git history 20c5228..9f2485d\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"Eleven selected deterministic GDDRAG, TaskGraph, TaskExecution, AgentRuntime/provider, process-runner, and testing-policy smoke/regression suites passed against the frozen clean tree. No Unity test was executed in this review environment.\",\n        \"path\": \"Pipeline/\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"observation\": \"Production GDDRAG is hash-current and integrity-valid with 41 chunks, correctly solving stale-index detection but not incorrect human canon.\",\n        \"path\": \"Pipeline/GDDRAG/integrity.py\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"gdd_iteration_concerns\": [\n      \"A GDD edit updates neither existing task contracts nor resource references automatically. Rebuilding RAG only makes retrieval agree with the edited document.\",\n      \"Every delivered task currently binds the whole GDD hash, so an unrelated wording or design edit forces global revalidation rather than scoped impact analysis.\",\n      \"There is no operational state for an active attempt when canon changes: continue under its frozen contract, pause, supersede, or replan are human-only decisions with no implemented transaction.\",\n      \"The existing scene-path contradiction proves one-time bootstrap correctness does not provide ongoing synchronization.\",\n      \"Introduce stable requirement IDs and per-task requirement hashes. On a GDD change, classify linked planned work as needing replan and linked delivered work as needing targeted revalidation; leave unrelated work current.\",\n      \"Freeze the task-contract/canon revision for each active attempt. At a checkpoint, a human or explicit policy decides whether a relevant GDD change supersedes that attempt. Never silently retarget work in progress.\"\n    ],\n    \"human_intervention_points\": [\n      \"Choose product priority and approve task-contract clarifications. NSC-003 especially needs decisions on input arbitration, click/hold behavior, arrival/cancellation, and pathing.\",\n      \"Approve GDD changes and decide whether active work continues, is superseded, or needs remediation.\",\n      \"Operate or authorize the licensed Unity host and resolve project locks/import state.\",\n      \"Perform Play Mode feel, visual readability, camera framing, scene/prefab, sorting, and interaction checks.\",\n      \"Review and merge changes; retain this authority until several consecutive deliveries are reliable.\",\n      \"Currently, manually invoke a writable coding agent because the production adapters are read-only.\",\n      \"Currently, manually assemble/promote Unity results and conformance records after integration.\",\n      \"Acquire, approve, import, and visually integrate art/audio assets.\",\n      \"Worth automating next only after repeated use: Unity command/result capture, evidence-manifest generation, branch/attempt recovery, and requirement-impact alerts.\"\n    ],\n    \"hypothetical_failure_solutions\": [\n      \"Parallel resource claims, multiple worktrees, merge queues, and GitHub synchronization protect a concurrency regime that does not exist yet.\",\n      \"Artifact Authority and Artifact GER protect future AI-authored design, but the current graph has no artifact task and no observed production blocker requiring it.\",\n      \"Progressive Decomposition addresses future coarse work; current execution fails before decomposition becomes the bottleneck.\",\n      \"Provider fallback and cross-provider review provenance do not advance a Unity ticket and are not yet production bottlenecks.\",\n      \"Much of AgentRuntime's adversarial JSON/subclass/path hardening protects theoretical provider-boundary attacks before providers have write authority.\",\n      \"The elaborate 15-auditor reconciliation/refinement/arbitration system protected a one-time bootstrap and should not become the routine response to GDD iteration.\",\n      \"Broad continuous-autonomy budgeting, backlog replenishment, and parallel scheduling are premature until one serial ticket can be delivered and recovered.\"\n    ],\n    \"missing_components\": [\n      \"One authoritative operational lifecycle ledger with attempt identity and explicit planned/running/validating/review/blocked/done/superseded states.\",\n      \"Evidence-derived dependency readiness tied to integrated delivery—not mutable task metadata.\",\n      \"A scoped writable implementer path with deterministic changed-file enforcement.\",\n      \"A real Unity-host execution adapter covering compilation, focused EditMode/PlayMode tests, and Windows build output.\",\n      \"Automatic evidence-manifest creation from actual Git and Unity results.\",\n      \"Branch/checkpoint/merge recovery that handles crashes and merged-but-unrecorded work idempotently.\",\n      \"Stable requirement-level GDD impact mapping.\",\n      \"Validation that task/resource/evidence paths still exist and agree with the current canonical scene registry.\",\n      \"Measured per-ticket elapsed time, human minutes, retries, token/cost use, and escaped-defect data.\"\n    ],\n    \"next_slice\": {\n      \"deliverables\": [\n        \"Human-freeze a narrow revision of NSC-005, resolving its duplicated/readability gates and specifying the smallest visible denied-mana feedback without expanding spell design.\",\n        \"Implement PlayerMana reset and denied-spend signaling plus the existing PlayerManaUI feedback consumer.\",\n        \"Extend PlayerMana Play Mode tests for reset, regeneration-delay reset, and denied-spend signaling.\",\n        \"Run the focused clean Unity PlayMode suite on the real host and perform one human readability check.\",\n        \"Merge through an ordinary branch and create one minimal delivery/evidence manifest using the existing mechanisms.\",\n        \"Record elapsed time, agent time, human minutes, retries, Unity import/test time, and manual edits.\"\n      ],\n      \"proof_of_value\": \"From a clean checkout, deliver a visibly improved, tested, merged gameplay capability within one working day, with no repository mutation from tests and no more than roughly 60–90 minutes of human orchestration. Repeatability—not another schema—is the first credible evidence that weeks can become days.\",\n      \"title\": \"Actual game production: deliver NSC-005 end to end\",\n      \"why\": \"NSC-005 extends an existing small component and existing Play Mode suite, avoids NSC-003's unresolved input design, and isolates the real delivery bottleneck. Use an ordinary writable coding-agent workflow and the existing clean test/evidence pieces; do not build a supervisor first.\"\n    },\n    \"observed_failure_solutions\": [\n      \"Repository-resident canon, contracts, logs, and decisions address real context/session loss and stale chat memory.\",\n      \"Production GDDRAG freshness/integrity addresses the actually stale July Assignment 4 index.\",\n      \"Reconciliation addressed stale Assignment 5 planning and found substantial semantic gaps before the initial graph was persisted.\",\n      \"GER runtime feedback solved camera defects missed by static evaluation.\",\n      \"The no-op progress guard and circuit breaker solve the observed refiner that claimed implementation without changing Assets.\",\n      \"The Unity testing policy and clean runner solve the observed passing test that rewrote a canonical scene.\",\n      \"Committed-scene conformance tests distinguish builder capability from actual serialized state, an observed source of false confidence.\",\n      \"Immutable run history and bounded recovery address timeouts/failures experienced while producing the reconciliation bootstrap.\"\n    ],\n    \"overall_verdict\": \"partially_unsound\",\n    \"overengineering\": [\n      \"Approximately 23,059 lines of executable Python/PowerShell across the production pipeline areas versus about 1,508 lines of C# under Assets/NoSafeCircle, excluding generated reconciliation outputs.\",\n      \"A 15-auditor reconciliation pass, streaming field repairs, conflict arbitration, and extensive recovery machinery for a 37-contract one-time bootstrap.\",\n      \"Provider-neutral runtime and two live adapters were proven through ArchitectureReview rather than a writable gameplay ticket.\",\n      \"Strict immutable invocation publication and deep hostile-value validation are disproportionate before any provider can write or execute approved commands.\",\n      \"Thirty-seven detailed contracts were produced before the project had a current lifecycle/readiness model, and their embedded repository evidence is already stale.\",\n      \"Multiple long context documents retain superseded milestone/status semantics, increasing maintenance and authority ambiguity.\",\n      \"Whole-GDD conformance invalidation creates expensive revalidation work instead of precise safety.\"\n    ],\n    \"state_and_authority_concerns\": [\n      \"Necessary boundaries: human-approved design canon; immutable task scope/revision; integrated Git tree; deterministic Unity/Git evidence; worker claims; and explicit human visual/design approval.\",\n      \"The AgentRuntime/TaskExecution separation is appropriate: generic invocation should not fabricate NSC task identity.\",\n      \"Tasks correctly should define work rather than completion, but removing status without introducing an operational lifecycle authority leaves the graph inert.\",\n      \"Reconciliation snapshots, bootstrap repository observations, task-embedded GDD excerpts, RAG chunks, and current-state documents duplicate facts and can disagree; the scene-path drift demonstrates this.\",\n      \"Git should remain implementation authority, but delivery needs a single evidence manifest and materialized lifecycle state rather than several indirect records.\",\n      \"Do not add GitHub as a second mutable authority. If added, make it a one-way projection of the local lifecycle ledger.\",\n      \"Human approval is currently correctly retained for interactive quality, but manually recording approval inside hand-authored evidence JSON is costly and error-prone.\"\n    ],\n    \"strong_decisions\": [\n      \"Use deterministic code for identity, hashes, graph structure, Git facts, test parsing, and safety checks.\",\n      \"Treat provider/agent output as claims rather than completion evidence.\",\n      \"Keep workers bounded and begin with one serial worker.\",\n      \"Make Unity/runtime evidence capable of overriding static semantic approval.\",\n      \"Fail tests when they mutate the repository, even if assertions pass.\",\n      \"Separate builder-generation tests from committed-scene conformance tests.\",\n      \"Keep reconciliation snapshots immutable and prevent them from directly rewriting living work.\",\n      \"Fail closed on stale RAG indexes while acknowledging retrieval is not complete canon.\",\n      \"Keep final design, visual, play-feel, and merge authority human-owned for now.\"\n    ],\n    \"structural_flaws\": [\n      \"There is no end-to-end state transition from selected contract to writable execution, Unity validation, merge, evidence publication, and dependent readiness.\",\n      \"The first break without more infrastructure is immediate: taskcontrol will not produce a ready task and both providers reject writes/commands. If a human bypasses that boundary, task/canon ambiguity and drift break correctness next.\",\n      \"Schema-v2 removed completion state but no lifecycle authority replaced it, so the dependency graph cannot schedule anything.\",\n      \"Moving-target synchronization is not implemented; a clean structural validation passes despite deleted canonical paths throughout the graph and GDD.\",\n      \"Conformance uses a global GDD hash instead of task-relevant requirement identities, making routine iteration globally expensive.\",\n      \"Graph validation checks syntax and relationships but not whether referenced Unity paths or repository evidence remain current.\",\n      \"The production runtime has been proven on architecture review, not implementation, repair, Unity, or recovery of a gameplay ticket.\",\n      \"The Unity lane is a human-invoked Windows PowerShell wrapper, not an integrated execution/recovery service; Windows build settings are still empty.\",\n      \"Several supposedly single-agent contracts assert design completeness that the repository's own current-state document later disputes, particularly NSC-003.\",\n      \"Canonical architecture/status documentation contradicts itself about readiness, milestone order, and scene authority.\",\n      \"No throughput telemetry establishes that the additional infrastructure reduces elapsed time or human effort.\"\n    ],\n    \"throughput_assessment\": \"The current system cannot turn weeks into days because it cannot autonomously start or deliver a gameplay task. Its strongest production proof is one camera feature whose static checks passed twice while Unity remained unusable, requiring two human runtime failures and three refinements. Since that work, HEAD ancestry contains 244 commits and roughly 115,877 added lines under Pipeline/Docs/Tasks but no new gameplay feature. The architecture may eventually reduce rediscovery, unsafe testing, and recovery cost, but major leverage requires repeated end-to-end delivery. A credible threshold is two or three consecutive small gameplay tickets delivered in a day each with bounded retries and under about 60–90 minutes of human orchestration per ticket.\",\n    \"verdict_reason\": \"Keep the bounded-worker, deterministic-validation, RAG freshness, Unity safety, and evidence ideas. Reject the current investment sequence and moving-canon model. The project has optimized review, provenance, and hypothetical autonomy risks before implementing the one transaction that creates value: safely turning an approved gameplay change into a tested, playable, merged increment.\"\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
