{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'rg -n -C 2 \"Failure is readable|failure is readable|low-mana|low mana|insufficient\" Docs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md'","aggregated_output":"183-- The player understands that enemies left alive remain a threat: leaving them alive means locking a door while they attack it, and later encountering them if that door breaks through.\r\n184-- Encounters use three to eight enemies and never exceed fifteen active enemies.\r\n185:- Failure is readable: poor positioning, low mana, using Force Wave without an immediate threat and leaving it unavailable when critical space is needed, or waiting too long.\r\n186-\r\n187-### Peer and Agent Review Revision\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"better_next_step_if_any\":\"The candidate first slice has a serious validity problem: NSC-005 can pass while avoiding nearly every disputed production boundary. Its current contract has no dependencies or locks, the tests instantiate only PlayerMana in memory, there is no spell or restart orchestrator, and the proposed human check drives a debug-only spend control. I’m now checking the actual Unity runner and state/evidence code to determine whether the synthesis’s “thin lane” is executable or merely another design document.\",\"failure_if_followed\":[\"A green NSC-005 receipt could be mistaken for proof of autonomous Unity delivery even though scene serialization, shared input, packages, build settings, dependency readiness, and real gameplay integration remain untested.\"],\"final_assessment\":\"synthesis_needs_revision\",\"hidden_assumptions\":[\"That a deliberately easy component/UI task is representative enough to validate the architecture.\",\"That a write-capable worker can be safely enabled without a defined enforcement boundary.\"],\"ignored_minority_arguments\":[\"Five reviewers favored movement because it exercises the actual Unity integration and unlocks downstream gameplay; the synthesis chose the three-reviewer mana position chiefly to isolate workflow plumbing.\"],\"reason\":\"Interim evidence favors revision; final judgment awaits the runner and authority checks.\",\"strongest_counter_case\":\"Ship the smallest player-visible movement slice through an ordinary human-operated worktree/Unity workflow, recording the lifecycle rather than building it first; use observed failures to decide which coordinator primitives deserve implementation.\",\"synthesis_weaknesses\":[\"The NSC-005 success test is not discriminating: the same result is likely achievable faster without the proposed architecture.\",\"The proposed slice validates debug scaffolding and future-facing APIs, not an integrated spell or restart loop.\"],\"what_would_change_my_mind\":[]}"}}
