{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba 'Pipeline/TaskGraph/current_conformance.py'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tfrom __future__ import annotations\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\t\"\"\"Deterministic current-conformance evaluation against committed HEAD.\"\"\"\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\timport json\r\n     6\tfrom dataclasses import asdict, dataclass\r\n     7\tfrom pathlib import Path\r\n     8\tfrom typing import Any\r\n     9\t\r\n    10\tfrom conformance_records import (\r\n    11\t    CANON_PATH,\r\n    12\t    CommittedRecord,\r\n    13\t    ConformanceRecordError,\r\n    14\t    GitRepository,\r\n    15\t    canonical_text_sha256,\r\n    16\t    load_committed_records,\r\n    17\t    semantic_json_sha256,\r\n    18\t)\r\n    19\t\r\n    20\tROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\r\n    21\t\r\n    22\t\r\n    23\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\n    24\tclass Finding:\r\n    25\t    code: str\r\n    26\t    message: str\r\n    27\t    record_id: str | None = None\r\n    28\t\r\n    29\t\r\n    30\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\n    31\tclass ConformanceState:\r\n    32\t    task_id: str\r\n    33\t    title: str\r\n    34\t    state: str\r\n    35\t    head_commit: str\r\n    36\t    head_tree: str\r\n    37\t    selected_record_id: str | None\r\n    38\t    findings: tuple[Finding, ...]\r\n    39\t    dirty_worktree: bool\r\n    40\t\r\n    41\t    def to_dict(self) -> dict[str, Any]:\r\n    42\t        value = asdict(self)\r\n    43\t        value[\"findings\"] = [asdict(item) for item in self.findings]\r\n    44\t        return value\r\n    45\t\r\n    46\t\r\n    47\tdef _json(repo: GitRepository, commit: str, path: str, label: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\r\n    48\t    try:\r\n    49\t        value = json.loads(repo.read(commit, path).decode(\"utf-8-sig\"))\r\n    50\t    except (UnicodeDecodeError, json.JSONDecodeError, ConformanceRecordError) as exc:\r\n    51\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"Unable to load {label} {path} at {commit}: {exc}\") from exc\r\n    52\t    if not isinstance(value, dict):\r\n    53\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{label} {path} must contain a JSON object.\")\r\n    54\t    return value\r\n    55\t\r\n    56\t\r\n    57\tdef resolve_committed_task(repo: GitRepository, head: str, selector: str) -> tuple[str, dict[str, Any]]:\r\n    58\t    raw = selector.strip()\r\n    59\t    if not raw:\r\n    60\t        raise ValueError(\"Task selector may not be blank.\")\r\n    61\t    direct = f\"Tasks/{raw.upper()}.yaml\"\r\n    62\t    if repo.exists(head, direct):\r\n    63\t        task = _json(repo, head, direct, \"task contract\")\r\n    64\t        return direct, task\r\n    65\t    matches: list[tuple[str, dict[str, Any]]] = []\r\n    66\t    for path in repo.files(head, \"Tasks\"):\r\n    67\t        if not path.endswith(\".yaml\"):\r\n    68\t            continue\r\n    69\t        task = _json(repo, head, path, \"task contract\")\r\n    70\t        if task.get(\"reconciliation_key\") == raw:\r\n    71\t            matches.append((path, task))\r\n    72\t    if len(matches) != 1:\r\n    73\t        raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task: {selector!r}. Use an NSC-* ID or reconciliation_key.\")\r\n    74\t    return matches[0]\r\n    75\t\r\n    76\t\r\n    77\tdef _finding(code: str, message: str, record: CommittedRecord | None = None) -> Finding:\r\n    78\t    return Finding(code, message, record.record_id if record else None)\r\n    79\t\r\n    80\t\r\n    81\tdef _validate_basis_graph(repo: GitRepository, records: list[CommittedRecord]) -> list[Finding]:\r\n    82\t    by_id = {record.record_id: record for record in records}\r\n    83\t    findings: list[Finding] = []\r\n    84\t    for record in records:\r\n    85\t        if record.data[\"record_type\"] != \"revalidation\":\r\n    86\t            continue\r\n    87\t        basis_id = record.data[\"revalidation\"][\"basis_record_id\"]\r\n    88\t        basis = by_id.get(basis_id)\r\n    89\t        if basis is None:\r\n    90\t            findings.append(_finding(\"basis_missing\", f\"Basis record {basis_id} does not exist.\", record))\r\n    91\t            continue\r\n    92\t        if basis.data[\"task_id\"] != record.data[\"task_id\"]:\r\n    93\t            findings.append(_finding(\"basis_task_mismatch\", \"Revalidation basis belongs to another task.\", record))\r\n    94\t        if not repo.is_ancestor(basis.validated_commit, record.validated_commit):\r\n    95\t            findings.append(_finding(\"basis_not_ancestor\", \"Basis validated commit is not an ancestor of revalidation commit.\", record))\r\n    96\t        seen = {record.record_id}\r\n    97\t        cursor = basis\r\n    98\t        while cursor.data[\"record_type\"] == \"revalidation\":\r\n    99\t            if cursor.record_id in seen:\r\n   100\t                findings.append(_finding(\"basis_cycle\", \"Revalidation basis chain contains a cycle.\", record))\r\n   101\t                break\r\n   102\t            seen.add(cursor.record_id)\r\n   103\t            next_id = cursor.data[\"revalidation\"][\"basis_record_id\"]\r\n   104\t            if next_id not in by_id:\r\n   105\t                break\r\n   106\t            cursor = by_id[next_id]\r\n   107\t    return findings\r\n   108\t\r\n   109\t\r\n   110\tdef _current_gate_ids(task: dict[str, Any]) -> list[str]:\r\n   111\t    gates = task.get(\"completion_gates\")\r\n   112\t    if not isinstance(gates, list):\r\n   113\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(\"Current task contract completion_gates must be a list.\")\r\n   114\t    result = [gate.get(\"gate_id\") if isinstance(gate, dict) else None for gate in gates]\r\n   115\t    if any(not isinstance(item, str) or not item for item in result) or len(set(result)) != len(result):\r\n   116\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(\"Current task contract has invalid or duplicate completion gate IDs.\")\r\n   117\t    return result  # type: ignore[return-value]\r\n   118\t\r\n   119\t\r\n   120\tdef _maximal(repo: GitRepository, records: list[CommittedRecord]) -> list[CommittedRecord]:\r\n   121\t    maximal: list[CommittedRecord] = []\r\n   122\t    for candidate in records:\r\n   123\t        if any(\r\n   124\t            other.record_id != candidate.record_id\r\n   125\t            and other.validated_commit != candidate.validated_commit\r\n   126\t            and repo.is_ancestor(candidate.validated_commit, other.validated_commit)\r\n   127\t            for other in records\r\n   128\t        ):\r\n   129\t            continue\r\n   130\t        maximal.append(candidate)\r\n   131\t    return sorted(maximal, key=lambda item: item.record_id)\r\n   132\t\r\n   133\t\r\n   134\tdef evaluate_current_conformance(root: Path | str = ROOT, selector: str = \"\") -> ConformanceState:\r\n   135\t    repo = GitRepository(root)\r\n   136\t    head = repo.head()\r\n   137\t    head_tree = repo.tree(head)\r\n   138\t    dirty = repo.dirty()\r\n   139\t    task_path, task = resolve_committed_task(repo, head, selector)\r\n   140\t    task_id = str(task.get(\"id\") or \"\")\r\n   141\t    title = str(task.get(\"title\") or \"\")\r\n   142\t\r\n   143\t    if task.get(\"schema_version\") != \"2.0\":\r\n   144\t        raise ValueError(f\"{task_id or task_path}: state requires a schema-v2 task contract at committed HEAD.\")\r\n   145\t\r\n   146\t    disposition = task.get(\"contract_disposition\")\r\n   147\t    if disposition in {\"cancelled\", \"superseded\"}:\r\n   148\t        return ConformanceState(task_id, title, disposition, head, head_tree, None,\r\n   149\t            (_finding(f\"contract_{disposition}\", f\"Contract disposition is {disposition}.\"),), dirty)\r\n   150\t    if task.get(\"kind\") == \"feature\" or task.get(\"execution_scope\") != \"single_agent\":\r\n   151\t        return ConformanceState(task_id, title, \"aggregate\", head, head_tree, None,\r\n   152\t            (_finding(\"non_executable_contract\", \"Feature or non-executable contract is aggregate.\"),), dirty)\r\n   153\t\r\n   154\t    try:\r\n   155\t        records = load_committed_records(repo, head, task_id)\r\n   156\t    except ConformanceRecordError as exc:\r\n   157\t        return ConformanceState(task_id, title, \"invalid_evidence\", head, head_tree, None,\r\n   158\t            (_finding(\"record_structure_invalid\", str(exc)),), dirty)\r\n   159\t    if not records:\r\n   160\t        return ConformanceState(task_id, title, \"not_delivered\", head, head_tree, None,\r\n   161\t            (_finding(\"no_committed_evidence\", \"No committed delivery, baseline, or revalidation record exists.\"),), dirty)\r\n   162\t\r\n   163\t    invalid = _validate_basis_graph(repo, records)\r\n   164\t    current_contract_hash = semantic_json_sha256(repo.read(head, task_path))\r\n   165\t    current_revision = task.get(\"contract_revision\")\r\n   166\t    current_canon_hash = canonical_text_sha256(repo.read(head, CANON_PATH))\r\n   167\t    current_gate_ids = _current_gate_ids(task)\r\n   168\t    conformant: list[CommittedRecord] = []\r\n   169\t    replan: list[CommittedRecord] = []\r\n   170\t    human: list[CommittedRecord] = []\r\n   171\t    stale: list[CommittedRecord] = []\r\n   172\t\r\n   173\t    for record in records:\r\n   174\t        data = record.data\r\n   175\t        state = data[\"validated_state\"]\r\n   176\t        try:\r\n   177\t            if repo.tree(state[\"commit\"]) != state[\"tree\"]:\r\n   178\t                invalid.append(_finding(\"validated_tree_mismatch\", \"Recorded tree does not match validated commit.\", record))\r\n   179\t                continue\r\n   180\t            contract = data[\"task_contract\"]\r\n   181\t            historical_task_raw = repo.read(state[\"commit\"], contract[\"path\"])\r\n   182\t            historical_task = json.loads(historical_task_raw.decode(\"utf-8-sig\"))\r\n   183\t            if semantic_json_sha256(historical_task) != contract[\"sha256\"] or historical_task.get(\"contract_revision\") != contract[\"revision\"] or historical_task.get(\"id\") != task_id:\r\n   184\t                invalid.append(_finding(\"recorded_contract_mismatch\", \"Recorded contract identity/hash is false at validated commit.\", record))\r\n   185\t                continue\r\n   186\t            canon = data[\"canon\"]\r\n   187\t            if canonical_text_sha256(repo.read(state[\"commit\"], canon[\"path\"])) != canon[\"sha256\"]:\r\n   188\t                invalid.append(_finding(\"recorded_canon_mismatch\", \"Recorded canon hash is false at validated commit.\", record))\r\n   189\t                continue\r\n   190\t            bad_surface = False\r\n   191\t            changed_surface = False\r\n   192\t            for surface in data[\"conformance_surfaces\"]:\r\n   193\t                if repo.blob(state[\"commit\"], surface[\"path\"]) != surface[\"blob_sha\"]:\r\n   194\t                    invalid.append(_finding(\"surface_validated_blob_mismatch\", f\"Surface {surface['path']} blob is false at validated commit.\", record))\r\n   195\t                    bad_surface = True\r\n   196\t                    break\r\n   197\t                if not repo.exists(head, surface[\"path\"]) or repo.blob(head, surface[\"path\"]) != surface[\"blob_sha\"]:\r\n   198\t                    changed_surface = True\r\n   199\t            if bad_surface:\r\n   200\t                continue\r\n   201\t            artifact_bad = False\r\n   202\t            for gate in data[\"gate_results\"]:\r\n   203\t                for evidence in gate[\"evidence\"]:\r\n   204\t                    artifact_prefix = f\"Pipeline/TaskGraph/evidence/{task_id}/artifacts/\"\r\n   205\t                    if not evidence[\"path\"].startswith(artifact_prefix):\r\n   206\t                        invalid.append(_finding(\"artifact_location_invalid\", f\"Gate artifact is outside {artifact_prefix}.\", record))\r\n   207\t                        artifact_bad = True\r\n   208\t                    elif not repo.exists(head, evidence[\"path\"]) or repo.blob(head, evidence[\"path\"]) != evidence[\"blob_sha\"]:\r\n   209\t                        invalid.append(_finding(\"artifact_blob_mismatch\", f\"Evidence artifact {evidence['path']} is absent or altered at HEAD.\", record))\r\n   210\t                        artifact_bad = True\r\n   211\t            if artifact_bad:\r\n   212\t                continue\r\n   213\t        except (ConformanceRecordError, json.JSONDecodeError, UnicodeDecodeError) as exc:\r\n   214\t            invalid.append(_finding(\"record_object_unavailable\", str(exc), record))\r\n   215\t            continue\r\n   216\t\r\n   217\t        if not repo.is_ancestor(state[\"commit\"], head):\r\n   218\t            stale.append(record)\r\n   219\t            continue\r\n   220\t\r\n   221\t        record_gate_ids = [gate[\"gate_id\"] for gate in data[\"gate_results\"]]\r\n   222\t        if record_gate_ids != current_gate_ids and set(record_gate_ids) != set(current_gate_ids):\r\n   223\t            invalid.append(_finding(\"completion_gate_set_mismatch\", \"Record does not contain exactly the current completion-gate set.\", record))\r\n   224\t            continue\r\n   225\t        contract_changed = contract[\"path\"] != task_path or contract[\"revision\"] != current_revision or contract[\"sha256\"] != current_contract_hash\r\n   226\t        if contract_changed:\r\n   227\t            replan.append(record)\r\n   228\t            continue\r\n   229\t        approval = data[\"human_approval\"]\r\n   230\t        if approval[\"required\"] and (approval[\"decision\"] != \"approved\" or not approval[\"approved_by\"].strip()):\r\n   231\t            human.append(record)\r\n   232\t            continue\r\n   233\t        if (not approval[\"required\"] and approval[\"decision\"] != \"not_required\"):\r\n   234\t            invalid.append(_finding(\"human_approval_contradictory\", \"Non-required approval must use not_required.\", record))\r\n   235\t            continue\r\n   236\t        if changed_surface or canon[\"path\"] != CANON_PATH or canon[\"sha256\"] != current_canon_hash:\r\n   237\t            stale.append(record)\r\n   238\t            continue\r\n   239\t        conformant.append(record)\r\n   240\t\r\n   241\t    if invalid:\r\n   242\t        return ConformanceState(task_id, title, \"invalid_evidence\", head, head_tree, None, tuple(invalid), dirty)\r\n   243\t    if conformant:\r\n   244\t        maximal = _maximal(repo, conformant)\r\n   245\t        if len(maximal) != 1:\r\n   246\t            ids = \", \".join(item.record_id for item in maximal)\r\n   247\t            return ConformanceState(task_id, title, \"ambiguous_evidence\", head, head_tree, None,\r\n   248\t                (_finding(\"multiple_maximal_current_records\", f\"Multiple maximal current-valid records: {ids}.\"),), dirty)\r\n   249\t        selected = maximal[0]\r\n   250\t        return ConformanceState(task_id, title, \"conformant\", head, head_tree, selected.record_id,\r\n   251\t            (_finding(\"current_record_selected\", \"Record is valid for current contract, canon, surfaces, gates, and artifacts.\", selected),), dirty)\r\n   252\t    for state_name, candidates, code, message in (\r\n   253\t        (\"needs_replan\", replan, \"contract_changed\", \"Current contract revision or semantic hash differs from prior evidence.\"),\r\n   254\t        (\"needs_human\", human, \"human_approval_missing\", \"Required human approval is missing.\"),\r\n   255\t        (\"needs_revalidation\", stale, \"evidence_stale\", \"Prior evidence exists but is not current for HEAD.\"),\r\n   256\t    ):\r\n   257\t        if candidates:\r\n   258\t            maximal = _maximal(repo, candidates)\r\n   259\t            selected = maximal[0] if len(maximal) == 1 else None\r\n   260\t            return ConformanceState(task_id, title, state_name, head, head_tree,\r\n   261\t                selected.record_id if selected else None, (_finding(code, message, selected),), dirty)\r\n   262\t    return ConformanceState(task_id, title, \"not_delivered\", head, head_tree, None,\r\n   263\t        (_finding(\"no_usable_evidence\", \"No usable committed evidence exists.\"),), dirty)\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba 'Pipeline/TaskGraph/conformance_records.py'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tfrom __future__ import annotations\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\t\"\"\"Schema and Git-object helpers for immutable conformance records.\"\"\"\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\timport hashlib\r\n     6\timport json\r\n     7\timport posixpath\r\n     8\timport re\r\n     9\timport subprocess\r\n    10\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\r\n    11\tfrom pathlib import Path\r\n    12\tfrom typing import Any\r\n    13\t\r\n    14\tSCHEMA_VERSION = \"1.0\"\r\n    15\tCANON_PATH = \"Docs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md\"\r\n    16\tEVIDENCE_ROOT = \"Pipeline/TaskGraph/evidence\"\r\n    17\tTASK_ID_RE = re.compile(r\"NSC-\\d{3,}\")\r\n    18\tHEX_RE = re.compile(r\"[0-9a-f]{40}\")\r\n    19\tFORBIDDEN_AUTHORITY_FIELDS = {\"status\", \"complete\", \"current\", \"ready\", \"authorized\"}\r\n    20\t\r\n    21\t\r\n    22\tclass ConformanceRecordError(RuntimeError):\r\n    23\t    pass\r\n    24\t\r\n    25\t\r\n    26\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\n    27\tclass CommittedRecord:\r\n    28\t    path: str\r\n    29\t    data: dict[str, Any]\r\n    30\t\r\n    31\t    @property\r\n    32\t    def record_id(self) -> str:\r\n    33\t        return self.data[\"record_id\"]\r\n    34\t\r\n    35\t    @property\r\n    36\t    def validated_commit(self) -> str:\r\n    37\t        return self.data[\"validated_state\"][\"commit\"]\r\n    38\t\r\n    39\t\r\n    40\tclass GitRepository:\r\n    41\t    def __init__(self, root: Path | str) -> None:\r\n    42\t        self.root = Path(root).resolve()\r\n    43\t\r\n    44\t    def _run(self, *args: str, check: bool = True) -> bytes:\r\n    45\t        result = subprocess.run(\r\n    46\t            [\"git\", *args], cwd=self.root, stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\r\n    47\t            stderr=subprocess.PIPE, check=False,\r\n    48\t        )\r\n    49\t        if check and result.returncode:\r\n    50\t            detail = result.stderr.decode(\"utf-8\", \"replace\").strip()\r\n    51\t            raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"git {' '.join(args)} failed: {detail}\")\r\n    52\t        return result.stdout\r\n    53\t\r\n    54\t    def head(self) -> str:\r\n    55\t        return self._run(\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").decode().strip()\r\n    56\t\r\n    57\t    def tree(self, commit: str) -> str:\r\n    58\t        return self._run(\"rev-parse\", f\"{commit}^{{tree}}\").decode().strip()\r\n    59\t\r\n    60\t    def read(self, commit: str, path: str) -> bytes:\r\n    61\t        safe_repository_path(path, \"Git object path\")\r\n    62\t        return self._run(\"show\", f\"{commit}:{path}\")\r\n    63\t\r\n    64\t    def blob(self, commit: str, path: str) -> str:\r\n    65\t        safe_repository_path(path, \"Git blob path\")\r\n    66\t        value = self._run(\"rev-parse\", f\"{commit}:{path}\").decode().strip()\r\n    67\t        if not HEX_RE.fullmatch(value):\r\n    68\t            raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path!r} is not a committed blob at {commit}.\")\r\n    69\t        return value\r\n    70\t\r\n    71\t    def exists(self, commit: str, path: str) -> bool:\r\n    72\t        safe_repository_path(path, \"Git object path\")\r\n    73\t        result = subprocess.run(\r\n    74\t            [\"git\", \"cat-file\", \"-e\", f\"{commit}:{path}\"], cwd=self.root,\r\n    75\t            stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, check=False,\r\n    76\t        )\r\n    77\t        return result.returncode == 0\r\n    78\t\r\n    79\t    def files(self, commit: str, prefix: str) -> list[str]:\r\n    80\t        safe_repository_path(prefix, \"Git tree prefix\")\r\n    81\t        output = self._run(\"ls-tree\", \"-r\", \"--name-only\", commit, \"--\", prefix)\r\n    82\t        return [line for line in output.decode(\"utf-8\").splitlines() if line]\r\n    83\t\r\n    84\t    def is_ancestor(self, older: str, newer: str) -> bool:\r\n    85\t        result = subprocess.run(\r\n    86\t            [\"git\", \"merge-base\", \"--is-ancestor\", older, newer], cwd=self.root,\r\n    87\t            stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, check=False,\r\n    88\t        )\r\n    89\t        return result.returncode == 0\r\n    90\t\r\n    91\t    def dirty(self) -> bool:\r\n    92\t        return bool(self._run(\"status\", \"--porcelain\"))\r\n    93\t\r\n    94\t    def path_history(self, commit: str, path: str) -> list[str]:\r\n    95\t        safe_repository_path(path, \"Git history path\")\r\n    96\t        output = self._run(\"log\", \"--format=%H\", commit, \"--\", path)\r\n    97\t        return [line for line in output.decode(\"utf-8\").splitlines() if line]\r\n    98\t\r\n    99\t\r\n   100\tdef safe_repository_path(value: Any, label: str) -> str:\r\n   101\t    if not isinstance(value, str) or not value:\r\n   102\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{label} must be a non-empty repository path.\")\r\n   103\t    if any(ord(character) < 32 for character in value):\r\n   104\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{label} contains a control character.\")\r\n   105\t    if value.startswith((\"/\", \"\\\\\")) or re.match(r\"^[A-Za-z]:\", value):\r\n   106\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{label} must be relative: {value!r}.\")\r\n   107\t    if \"\\\\\" in value or posixpath.normpath(value) != value or value in {\".\", \"..\"}:\r\n   108\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{label} is not a canonical repository path: {value!r}.\")\r\n   109\t    if any(part in {\"\", \".\", \"..\"} for part in value.split(\"/\")):\r\n   110\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{label} contains path traversal: {value!r}.\")\r\n   111\t    return value\r\n   112\t\r\n   113\t\r\n   114\tdef semantic_json_sha256(raw: bytes | str | Any) -> str:\r\n   115\t    if isinstance(raw, bytes):\r\n   116\t        value = json.loads(raw.decode(\"utf-8-sig\"))\r\n   117\t    elif isinstance(raw, str):\r\n   118\t        value = json.loads(raw.lstrip(\"\\ufeff\"))\r\n   119\t    else:\r\n   120\t        value = raw\r\n   121\t    canonical = json.dumps(\r\n   122\t        value, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"), allow_nan=False\r\n   123\t    )\r\n   124\t    return hashlib.sha256(canonical.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\r\n   125\t\r\n   126\t\r\n   127\tdef canonical_text_sha256(raw: bytes | str) -> str:\r\n   128\t    text = raw.decode(\"utf-8-sig\") if isinstance(raw, bytes) else raw.lstrip(\"\\ufeff\")\r\n   129\t    text = text.replace(\"\\r\\n\", \"\\n\").replace(\"\\r\", \"\\n\")\r\n   130\t    return hashlib.sha256(text.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\r\n   131\t\r\n   132\t\r\n   133\tdef _object(value: Any, label: str, fields: set[str]) -> dict[str, Any]:\r\n   134\t    if not isinstance(value, dict):\r\n   135\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{label} must be an object.\")\r\n   136\t    extra = set(value) - fields\r\n   137\t    missing = fields - set(value)\r\n   138\t    if extra or missing:\r\n   139\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(\r\n   140\t            f\"{label} fields differ from schema (missing={sorted(missing)}, extra={sorted(extra)}).\"\r\n   141\t        )\r\n   142\t    return value\r\n   143\t\r\n   144\t\r\n   145\tdef _text(value: Any, label: str, *, allow_empty: bool = False) -> str:\r\n   146\t    if not isinstance(value, str) or (not allow_empty and not value.strip()):\r\n   147\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{label} must be a {'string' if allow_empty else 'non-empty string'}.\")\r\n   148\t    return value\r\n   149\t\r\n   150\t\r\n   151\tdef _sha(value: Any, label: str) -> str:\r\n   152\t    value = _text(value, label)\r\n   153\t    if not HEX_RE.fullmatch(value):\r\n   154\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{label} must be a lowercase 40-character Git SHA.\")\r\n   155\t    return value\r\n   156\t\r\n   157\t\r\n   158\tdef validate_record_shape(record: Any, path: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\r\n   159\t    common = {\r\n   160\t        \"schema_version\", \"record_type\", \"record_id\", \"task_id\", \"task_contract\",\r\n   161\t        \"canon\", \"validated_state\", \"conformance_surfaces\", \"gate_results\",\r\n   162\t        \"human_approval\", \"recorded_at\",\r\n   163\t    }\r\n   164\t    if not isinstance(record, dict):\r\n   165\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}: record must be an object.\")\r\n   166\t    forbidden = FORBIDDEN_AUTHORITY_FIELDS.intersection(record)\r\n   167\t    if forbidden:\r\n   168\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}: mutable authority fields are forbidden: {sorted(forbidden)}.\")\r\n   169\t    record_type = record.get(\"record_type\")\r\n   170\t    specific = (\r\n   171\t        \"delivery\" if record_type == \"delivery\"\r\n   172\t        else \"baseline\" if record_type == \"baseline\"\r\n   173\t        else \"revalidation\" if record_type == \"revalidation\"\r\n   174\t        else None\r\n   175\t    )\r\n   176\t    if specific is None:\r\n   177\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}: record_type must be delivery, baseline, or revalidation.\")\r\n   178\t    _object(record, path, common | {specific})\r\n   179\t    if record[\"schema_version\"] != SCHEMA_VERSION:\r\n   180\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}: unsupported schema_version {record['schema_version']!r}.\")\r\n   181\t\r\n   182\t    task_id = _text(record[\"task_id\"], f\"{path}.task_id\")\r\n   183\t    if not TASK_ID_RE.fullmatch(task_id):\r\n   184\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}: invalid task_id {task_id!r}.\")\r\n   185\t    record_id = _text(record[\"record_id\"], f\"{path}.record_id\")\r\n   186\t    prefix = {\"delivery\": \"DEL-\", \"baseline\": \"BASE-\", \"revalidation\": \"REV-\"}[record_type]\r\n   187\t    if not record_id.startswith(f\"{prefix}{task_id}-\"):\r\n   188\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}: record_id prefix/task identity mismatch.\")\r\n   189\t    expected_prefix = f\"{EVIDENCE_ROOT}/{task_id}/records/\"\r\n   190\t    if not path.startswith(expected_prefix) or path != f\"{expected_prefix}{record_id}.json\":\r\n   191\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}: record path, task_id, filename, and record_id disagree.\")\r\n   192\t\r\n   193\t    contract = _object(record[\"task_contract\"], f\"{path}.task_contract\", {\"path\", \"revision\", \"sha256\"})\r\n   194\t    safe_repository_path(contract[\"path\"], f\"{path}.task_contract.path\")\r\n   195\t    if isinstance(contract[\"revision\"], bool) or not isinstance(contract[\"revision\"], int) or contract[\"revision\"] < 1:\r\n   196\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}.task_contract.revision must be a positive integer.\")\r\n   197\t    if not re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{64}\", _text(contract[\"sha256\"], f\"{path}.task_contract.sha256\")):\r\n   198\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}.task_contract.sha256 must be lowercase SHA-256.\")\r\n   199\t    canon = _object(record[\"canon\"], f\"{path}.canon\", {\"path\", \"sha256\"})\r\n   200\t    safe_repository_path(canon[\"path\"], f\"{path}.canon.path\")\r\n   201\t    if not re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{64}\", _text(canon[\"sha256\"], f\"{path}.canon.sha256\")):\r\n   202\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}.canon.sha256 must be lowercase SHA-256.\")\r\n   203\t    state = _object(record[\"validated_state\"], f\"{path}.validated_state\", {\"commit\", \"tree\"})\r\n   204\t    _sha(state[\"commit\"], f\"{path}.validated_state.commit\")\r\n   205\t    _sha(state[\"tree\"], f\"{path}.validated_state.tree\")\r\n   206\t\r\n   207\t    surfaces = record[\"conformance_surfaces\"]\r\n   208\t    if not isinstance(surfaces, list):\r\n   209\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}.conformance_surfaces must be a list.\")\r\n   210\t    surface_paths: set[str] = set()\r\n   211\t    for index, raw in enumerate(surfaces):\r\n   212\t        surface = _object(raw, f\"{path}.conformance_surfaces[{index}]\", {\"path\", \"blob_sha\", \"role\"})\r\n   213\t        item_path = safe_repository_path(surface[\"path\"], f\"{path}.conformance_surfaces[{index}].path\")\r\n   214\t        if item_path in surface_paths:\r\n   215\t            raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}: duplicate conformance surface path {item_path!r}.\")\r\n   216\t        surface_paths.add(item_path)\r\n   217\t        _sha(surface[\"blob_sha\"], f\"{path}.conformance_surfaces[{index}].blob_sha\")\r\n   218\t        _text(surface[\"role\"], f\"{path}.conformance_surfaces[{index}].role\")\r\n   219\t\r\n   220\t    gates = record[\"gate_results\"]\r\n   221\t    if not isinstance(gates, list):\r\n   222\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}.gate_results must be a list.\")\r\n   223\t    gate_ids: set[str] = set()\r\n   224\t    for index, raw in enumerate(gates):\r\n   225\t        gate = _object(raw, f\"{path}.gate_results[{index}]\", {\"gate_id\", \"result\", \"evidence\", \"notes\"})\r\n   226\t        gate_id = _text(gate[\"gate_id\"], f\"{path}.gate_results[{index}].gate_id\")\r\n   227\t        if gate_id in gate_ids:\r\n   228\t            raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}: duplicate gate_id {gate_id!r}.\")\r\n   229\t        gate_ids.add(gate_id)\r\n   230\t        if gate[\"result\"] != \"pass\":\r\n   231\t            raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}: only a pass gate result can establish conformance.\")\r\n   232\t        if not isinstance(gate[\"evidence\"], list):\r\n   233\t            raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}.gate_results[{index}].evidence must be a list.\")\r\n   234\t        for evidence_index, raw_evidence in enumerate(gate[\"evidence\"]):\r\n   235\t            evidence = _object(raw_evidence, f\"{path}.gate_results[{index}].evidence[{evidence_index}]\", {\"path\", \"blob_sha\"})\r\n   236\t            safe_repository_path(evidence[\"path\"], f\"{path}.gate_results[{index}].evidence[{evidence_index}].path\")\r\n   237\t            _sha(evidence[\"blob_sha\"], f\"{path}.gate_results[{index}].evidence[{evidence_index}].blob_sha\")\r\n   238\t        _text(gate[\"notes\"], f\"{path}.gate_results[{index}].notes\", allow_empty=True)\r\n   239\t\r\n   240\t    approval = _object(record[\"human_approval\"], f\"{path}.human_approval\", {\"required\", \"decision\", \"approved_by\", \"notes\"})\r\n   241\t    if not isinstance(approval[\"required\"], bool):\r\n   242\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}.human_approval.required must be boolean.\")\r\n   243\t    if approval[\"decision\"] not in {\"approved\", \"not_required\"}:\r\n   244\t        raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}.human_approval.decision is unsupported.\")\r\n   245\t    _text(approval[\"approved_by\"], f\"{path}.human_approval.approved_by\", allow_empty=True)\r\n   246\t    _text(approval[\"notes\"], f\"{path}.human_approval.notes\", allow_empty=True)\r\n   247\t    _text(record[\"recorded_at\"], f\"{path}.recorded_at\")\r\n   248\t\r\n   249\t    if record_type == \"delivery\":\r\n   250\t        delivery = _object(record[\"delivery\"], f\"{path}.delivery\", {\"base_commit\", \"candidate_commit\", \"integrated_commit\", \"integrated_tree\"})\r\n   251\t        for field in delivery:\r\n   252\t            _sha(delivery[field], f\"{path}.delivery.{field}\")\r\n   253\t        if state[\"commit\"] != delivery[\"integrated_commit\"] or state[\"tree\"] != delivery[\"integrated_tree\"]:\r\n   254\t            raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}: delivery integrated and validated states must match.\")\r\n   255\t    elif record_type == \"baseline\":\r\n   256\t        baseline = _object(record[\"baseline\"], f\"{path}.baseline\", {\"reason_type\", \"summary\"})\r\n   257\t        if baseline[\"reason_type\"] != \"pre_evidence_existing_implementation\":\r\n   258\t            raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}.baseline.reason_type is unsupported.\")\r\n   259\t        _text(baseline[\"summary\"], f\"{path}.baseline.summary\")\r\n   260\t    else:\r\n   261\t        revalidation = _object(record[\"revalidation\"], f\"{path}.revalidation\", {\"basis_record_id\", \"reason_type\", \"summary\"})\r\n   262\t        _text(revalidation[\"basis_record_id\"], f\"{path}.revalidation.basis_record_id\")\r\n   263\t        if revalidation[\"reason_type\"] not in {\"code_change\", \"gdd_change\", \"contract_change\", \"periodic\", \"manual\"}:\r\n   264\t            raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"{path}.revalidation.reason_type is unsupported.\")\r\n   265\t        _text(revalidation[\"summary\"], f\"{path}.revalidation.summary\")\r\n   266\t    return record\r\n   267\t\r\n   268\t\r\n   269\tdef load_committed_records(repo: GitRepository, head: str, task_id: str) -> list[CommittedRecord]:\r\n   270\t    prefix = f\"{EVIDENCE_ROOT}/{task_id}/records\"\r\n   271\t    records: list[CommittedRecord] = []\r\n   272\t    ids: set[str] = set()\r\n   273\t    for path in repo.files(head, prefix):\r\n   274\t        if not path.endswith(\".json\"):\r\n   275\t            raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"Unsupported committed record file: {path}.\")\r\n   276\t        if len(repo.path_history(head, path)) != 1:\r\n   277\t            raise ConformanceRecordError(\r\n   278\t                f\"Immutable record {path} was modified, deleted/recreated, or has ambiguous history.\"\r\n   279\t            )\r\n   280\t        try:\r\n   281\t            value = json.loads(repo.read(head, path).decode(\"utf-8-sig\"))\r\n   282\t        except (UnicodeDecodeError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\r\n   283\t            raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"Unable to parse committed record {path}: {exc}\") from exc\r\n   284\t        validate_record_shape(value, path)\r\n   285\t        if value[\"record_id\"] in ids:\r\n   286\t            raise ConformanceRecordError(f\"Duplicate record_id {value['record_id']!r}.\")\r\n   287\t        ids.add(value[\"record_id\"])\r\n   288\t        records.append(CommittedRecord(path, value))\r\n   289\t    return records\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba 'Pipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Provider-neutral AgentRuntime\n     2\t\n     3\tThis runtime foundation extracts the reusable orchestration ideas demonstrated by Assignment 3: fresh bounded invocations, explicit request/result handoffs, semantic capability limits, structured output, normalized failures, and immutable run artifacts. `AgentCrew/` and `Assignment6GER/` remain unchanged historical coursework evidence; this package neither imports nor retrofits them.\n     4\t\n     5\t`AgentInvocationRequest` describes one generic bounded invocation: run identity, role, prompt, repository context, semantic capabilities, write policy, output shape, capability-class selection, budgets, and provider configuration. It has no No Safe Circle task identity and no dependency on `Tasks/*.yaml`. `AgentResult` describes only an invocation outcome and provider/agent claims. Task identity belongs to `Pipeline/TaskExecution`; delivery, conformance, readiness, authorization, integration, repository changes, command execution, and test success remain decisions for higher deterministic repository, test, and evidence systems.\n     6\t\n     7\tAll retained request, result, and runtime-configuration JSON values are recursively validated and frozen. Runtime configuration invariants apply equally to direct construction, dictionaries, and strict JSON loading. Only exact built-in JSON null, booleans, integers, finite numbers, valid UTF-8 strings, lists/tuples, dictionaries, and the runtime's own frozen mapping proxies are accepted. Polymorphic container and text subclasses are rejected so provider callbacks cannot run during validation or make publication disagree with the validated snapshot. Cycles and nesting deeper than the conservative 64-container limit are rejected deterministically. `to_dict()` methods return detached mutable copies. The runner accepts only the exact `AgentInvocationRequest`, `RuntimeConfiguration`, and `ProviderInvocationResponse` types; requests additionally require exact `WriteBoundaries` and `Budgets`, while results require exact `Usage`. Base serializers are called non-polymorphically, preventing subclass serialization or response-container overrides at these trust boundaries.\n     8\t\n     9\tIdentifiers use conservative lowercase ASCII forms: run IDs are 1–64 character lowercase alphanumeric/hyphen slugs, while roles and configuration keys begin with a lowercase letter and use lowercase letters, digits, underscores, and separated hyphens. Every serialized operational string must be UTF-8 encodable. Repository paths are already-normalized, relative POSIX paths and additionally reject surrogates, NUL, ASCII controls, DEL, line breaks, tabs, Windows-forbidden characters, alternate-data-stream colons, trailing dots/spaces, and reserved Windows device names. Write-boundary components are compared conservatively and case-insensitively while remaining component-aware; denied boundaries override allowed ones. Budget maxima are 1,000 turns, 86,400 seconds, and 10,000,000 tokens.\n    10\t\n    11\tProvider adapters expose an identifier, accept the common request plus a configured concrete model, return structured output and raw log text separately, and normalize provider failures. They translate invocation mechanics only. They may never write task/evidence/readiness state or declare delivery, conformance, readiness, or authorization. Live-provider adapters must pass the same contract suite.\n    12\t\n    13\t`ProviderOutputInvalid` represents provider output from which an adapter could not produce a structured-output candidate. `AgentRunner` normalizes it to `schema_error`. This is distinct from a successfully parsed candidate that the runner later rejects through central schema validation, although both outcomes normalize to `schema_error`. `ProviderRequestRejected` represents a provider that cannot safely honor a selected request policy and normalizes to `invalid_request` after provider/model selection. Exact provider raw output is retained in `provider.log` when it is valid. Neither exception establishes deterministic correctness, delivery, conformance, readiness, authorization, approval, integration, or test-success authority.\n    14\t\n    15\t`FakeProvider` is deterministic and performs no network, command, version-control, engine, or repository access. It exercises success, provider failure, invalid provider output, timeout, permission denial, budget exhaustion, and centrally detected schema failure.\n    16\t\n    17\t`ClaudeCodeProvider` now includes **Stage 4B.2 — Practical Repository Read/Search**. It supports the empty capability set, `repository_read`, `repository_search`, and their combination. Empty-capability invocations retain the Stage 4B behavior: a new empty temporary directory outside the repository with no tools. Repository-capable invocations run against the actual source repository root (`/workspace` in Docker): `repository_read` exposes native `Read`, while `repository_search` exposes native `Glob` and `Grep`. Repository write, approved command execution, and every non-null token limit remain rejected before launch.\n    18\t\n    19\tNonempty `context_paths` remain invalid without a repository capability. With a repository capability they are accepted as validated repository-relative invocation hints and added to a generated repository-context section in the effective provider prompt without mutating the `AgentInvocationRequest`. They are guidance, not a hardened read allowlist. This trusted single-user boundary intentionally prioritizes useful access to the current working tree; ADR-038 records the accepted limited risk.\n    20\t\n    21\tClaude receives the exact concrete configured model with no alias or fallback, native `--max-turns` equal to the request's required positive `turn_limit`, and the independent external hard `timeout_seconds` enforced by the shared subprocess transport. The prompt travels through stdin, while the compact output schema, exact `--tools` value, and explicit `Bash`, `Edit`, `Write`, `NotebookEdit`, `WebSearch`, and `WebFetch` denial travel as direct argv elements with `shell=False`; no `--allowedTools` argument is emitted. The shared standard-library transport captures stdout and stderr concurrently through `communicate`, creates a new process group/session, terminates the group on timeout with bounded cleanup, and preserves available partial output. Deterministic adapter and AgentRunner integration tests inject a fake process runner and never launch Claude. The opt-in `tests/claude_repository_read_search_live_smoke.py` requires `NSC_RUN_CLAUDE_REPOSITORY_SMOKE=1`; normal deterministic runs skip live Claude access.\n    22\t\n    23\tClaude stdout is decoded strictly as UTF-8 and retained exactly as `provider.log`. A successful response must be one JSON result envelope with exact built-in status metadata: `type=result`, `is_error=false`, `subtype=success`, `terminal_reason=completed`, and a present `structured_output`; `stop_reason=tool_use` is acceptable. Missing or malformed status or permission-denial metadata is `ProviderOutputInvalid`. A nonempty, exact-list `permission_denials`, other well-formed unsuccessful result envelopes, and nonzero exits are provider failures. `ProviderTransportError` covers local process/transcript failures, invalid usage metadata, and unexpected stderr on a zero exit, and `AgentRunner` normalizes it to `internal_error` while retaining any valid exact raw log. Timeouts remain `timeout` and retain valid partial stdout.\n    24\t\n    25\tNormalized Claude usage prefers all `modelUsage` entries, including cache-read and cache-creation input tokens, and otherwise falls back conservatively to top-level `usage`. An explicitly present empty `modelUsage` object and malformed, negative, boolean, non-finite, or inconsistent usage fail closed as transport errors.\n    26\t\n    27\tEach caller-supplied run root receives a uniquely and atomically created `<run_id>/` containing canonical `request.json`, `provider.log`, and `result.json`. JSON artifacts use strict finite JSON, deterministic key ordering, UTF-8 bytes, LF line endings, and one trailing LF. `provider.log` is the provider's exact raw text and is not decorated with runtime diagnostics. Each file is written and fsynced as a temporary file, then atomically hard-linked into place only if its destination does not exist; failed publication cleans its temporary file and cannot overwrite existing bytes. Existing run directories are never reused. A run directory is an audit artifact, not evidence of correctness.\n    28\t\n    29\tAfter a valid request exists, the runner creates the run directory and publishes `request.json` before resolving provider configuration. Unknown configurations, unavailable configured providers, and missing capability mappings therefore produce a preserved failed `result.json` classified as `invalid_request` without invoking a provider. Provider and model are null only when this pre-invocation selection did not succeed; post-selection failures retain the selected values.\n    30\t\n    31\tEvery failed `AgentResult` has a non-whitespace, non-authoritative `failure_message` and must keep `structured_output` null so rejected output cannot appear accepted; successful results leave the diagnostic null or empty. This diagnostic preserves configuration, provider-exception, schema-validation, and rejected-metadata details. It never establishes delivery, conformance, readiness, authorization, test success, or approval. Provider invocation failures and structured-output validation are normalized separately: unexpected ordinary provider exceptions are `internal_error`, while invalid structured JSON or schema mismatch is `schema_error`. Provider responses are field-snapshotted exactly once after their exact-type check. Structured output is immediately detached and frozen, and that same snapshot is both schema-validated and retained. Valid usage and execution/change/test claims survive a post-invocation `schema_error`, while rejected structured output remains null. Invalid raw logs are replaced by an empty log and a safe diagnostic; malformed exception text cannot block artifact publication. Process-control exceptions are not swallowed.\n    32\t\n    33\tStructured output supports only these JSON Schema features: the object, array, string, integer, number, boolean, and null types; `properties`; `required`; boolean `additionalProperties`; `items`; `enum`; and finite numeric `minimum`/`maximum` on integer or number schemas. Unknown keywords fail closed. The runner—not an adapter—validates successful output.\n    34\t\n    35\t`OpenAICodexProvider` supports empty capability, repository read, repository search, and combined read/search requests. Repository access requires an explicit externally enforced read-only construction profile; empty-capability requests use a temporary directory outside the repository. It forwards the selected concrete model, sends prompts by stdin, preserves exact JSONL stdout, parses the final-output file, uses the last completed-turn usage event, and enforces `min(timeout_seconds, turn_limit * 30)`. ArchitectureReview supplies the external Docker read-only profile. Repository writes, approved command execution, non-null token limits, fallback, and production role orchestration remain unsupported.\n    36\t\n    37\tThe runtime still has no crew roles/prompts, engine execution, GER integration, task selection, version-control workflow, TaskGraph evidence creation, conformance/readiness derivation, or dispatch authorization.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
