{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba 'Docs/AI-Pipeline/04_EXECUTION_GER_VALIDATION_CONTEXT.md'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Context 4 — Agent Crew + GER + Validation / Repair Loop\n     2\t\n     3\t## Goal\n     4\t\n     5\tTurn ticket implementation into a reliable bounded execution pipeline.\n     6\t\n     7\tPrerequisites: supervisor, worktree/branch/PR, and task context.\n     8\t\n     9\t## Assignment 3 Crew Placement\n    10\t\n    11\tThe crew belongs inside ticket execution:\n    12\t\n    13\t```text\n    14\tPersistent Task Graph chooses WHAT\n    15\t       ↓\n    16\tTicket Context\n    17\t       ↓\n    18\tPlanner\n    19\t       ↓\n    20\tImplementer\n    21\t       ↓\n    22\tValidator\n    23\t```\n    24\t\n    25\tDo not let the crew rebuild the global roadmap.\n    26\t\n    27\t## Planner\n    28\t\n    29\tInput: task artifact, acceptance criteria, relevant GDD chunks, relevant project state/files.\n    30\t\n    31\tOutput: small implementation plan, expected files, validation plan.\n    32\t\n    33\tNo scope broadening.\n    34\t\n    35\t## Implementer\n    36\t\n    37\tImplement only the selected ticket. If a new substantial prerequisite is discovered, stop and report a blocker instead of silently absorbing another ticket.\n    38\t\n    39\t## Deterministic Validation First\n    40\t\n    41\tRun local checks before asking another model:\n    42\t\n    43\t- `git diff --check`\n    44\t- prohibited-file/path checks\n    45\t- scope checks\n    46\t- static checks\n    47\t- task graph checks\n    48\t- unit tests\n    49\t- Unity compile\n    50\t- Unity EditMode tests\n    51\t- Unity PlayMode tests\n    52\t\n    53\t## Unity Validation\n    54\t\n    55\tEventually run Unity command-line/batch validation on the real development machine. Do not treat a Docker environment without Unity as final runtime truth.\n    56\t\n    57\tProduce machine-readable test results.\n    58\t\n    59\t## Fresh AI Diff Review\n    60\t\n    61\tAfter deterministic validation, give a fresh reviewer only:\n    62\t\n    63\t- task contract\n    64\t- acceptance criteria\n    65\t- relevant GDD evidence\n    66\t- git diff\n    67\t- deterministic test results\n    68\t\n    69\tAsk whether the diff satisfies the ticket without exceeding scope.\n    70\t\n    71\t## Repair Loop\n    72\t\n    73\t```text\n    74\tfailure evidence → Implementer repair → deterministic tests → AI diff review\n    75\t```\n    76\t\n    77\tLimit retries.\n    78\t\n    79\t## Assignment 6 — GER\n    80\t\n    81\tUse GER for generated game content/artifacts:\n    82\t\n    83\t```text\n    84\tGenerator\n    85\t ↓\n    86\tEvaluator\n    87\t ↓ PASS → approved artifact\n    88\t\n    89\tFAIL\n    90\t ↓\n    91\tRefiner\n    92\t ↓\n    93\tEvaluator\n    94\t ↓\n    95\t(retry limit)\n    96\t ↓\n    97\tCircuit Breaker\n    98\t ↓\n    99\tNeeds Human Review\n   100\t```\n   101\t\n   102\tRAG feeds the evaluator with exact GDD rules.\n   103\t\n   104\tPossible generated artifact directories:\n   105\t\n   106\t```text\n   107\tArtifacts/\n   108\t  Encounters/\n   109\t  ArtSpecs/\n   110\t  Tutorials/\n   111\t  Balance/\n   112\t  Dialogue/\n   113\t```\n   114\t\n   115\tA generated artifact can be a dependency of a later code/content task.\n   116\t\n   117\tExample:\n   118\t\n   119\t```text\n   120\tNSC-035 Generate Bone Archive Encounter\n   121\t        ↓\n   122\tapproved artifact\n   123\t        ↓\n   124\tNSC-040 Implement Bone Archive Encounter\n   125\t```\n   126\t\n   127\t## Cost / Circuit Breakers\n   128\t\n   129\tPer ticket define limits such as max agent runs, max repair attempts, runtime, and budget. Escalate on GDD ambiguity, repeated test/GER failure, architecture-changing dependencies, scope expansion, Unity conflicts, or budget exhaustion.\n   130\t\n   131\t## Completion Definition\n   132\t\n   133\t```text\n   134\timplementation → deterministic tests → Unity tests → fresh AI review → PR ready → merge → task complete\n   135\t```\n   136\t\n   137\tA worker saying “implemented” is not completion.\n   138\t\n   139\t## Completion Criteria\n   140\t\n   141\tA ticket reliably reaches either `Merged / Done` or `Needs Human Review`, with bounded spending and clear evidence.\n   142\t\n   143\t## Next\n   144\t\n   145\tContinue with `05_CONTINUOUS_AUTONOMY_CONTEXT.md`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
