{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba 'Docs/AI-Pipeline/05_CONTINUOUS_AUTONOMY_CONTEXT.md'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Context 5 — Continuous Autonomous Development\n     2\t\n     3\t## Goal\n     4\t\n     5\tOnce one-ticket execution is reliable, let the system continue through the safe ready backlog with minimal supervision.\n     6\t\n     7\t## Main Loop\n     8\t\n     9\t```python\n    10\twhile True:\n    11\t    ready = taskctl.ready_ranked()\n    12\t\n    13\t    if not ready:\n    14\t        run_planning_reconciliation_or_pause()\n    15\t        continue\n    16\t\n    17\t    task = select_first_safe_task(ready)\n    18\t    result = execute_ticket(task)\n    19\t\n    20\t    if result == \"merged\":\n    21\t        taskctl.recalculate()\n    22\t        continue\n    23\t\n    24\t    if result == \"blocked\":\n    25\t        record_blocker()\n    26\t        continue_with_another_ready_task()\n    27\t\n    28\t    if result == \"needs_human\":\n    29\t        surface_to_user()\n    30\t        continue_with_other_safe_work_if_allowed()\n    31\t```\n    32\t\n    33\t## Principle\n    34\t\n    35\tThe supervisor is autonomous. Claude is a bounded/replaceable worker per ticket.\n    36\t\n    37\t## Newly Discovered Blockers\n    38\t\n    39\tIf Fireball discovers a substantial missing Projectile Collision prerequisite:\n    40\t\n    41\t1. report blocker\n    42\t2. propose/create a new task\n    43\t3. validate/add dependency\n    44\t4. mark Fireball blocked\n    45\t5. preserve its branch/PR if useful\n    46\t6. scheduler chooses another safe ready task\n    47\t\n    48\tDo not silently implement both goals.\n    49\t\n    50\t## Planning / Backlog Replenishment\n    51\t\n    52\tWhen the ready queue is empty or backlog coverage is low:\n    53\t\n    54\t```text\n    55\tGDD RAG + current project scanner + existing tasks\n    56\t ↓\n    57\trequirements reconciliation\n    58\t ↓\n    59\tproposed task artifacts/dependencies\n    60\t ↓\n    61\tgraph validation\n    62\t ↓\n    63\tplanning PR\n    64\t```\n    65\t\n    66\tInitially require human approval for roadmap/task-graph changes.\n    67\t\n    68\t## GDD Change Detection\n    69\t\n    70\tTrack a GDD hash/version. On material changes, invalidate relevant caches and reconcile affected requirements/tasks rather than blindly rebuilding everything.\n    71\t\n    72\t## GitHub Dashboard\n    73\t\n    74\tThe user should be able to see Backlog, Ready, In Progress, Blocked, Validating, Needs Review, and Done, with an Issue/PR/dependency/validation trail for active work.\n    75\t\n    76\t## Merge Safety\n    77\t\n    78\tBefore final validation, update the ticket branch against current main and rerun validation. Consider a merge queue only once multiple workers exist.\n    79\t\n    80\t## Parallelism\n    81\t\n    82\tOnly after single-worker reliability. Scheduler must reject overlapping conflict/resource claims. Be conservative with Unity scenes, prefabs, ProjectSettings, and shared builder scripts.\n    83\t\n    84\t## Observability\n    85\t\n    86\tPersist run records outside model context:\n    87\t\n    88\t```text\n    89\tRuns/\n    90\t  NSC-014/\n    91\t    <run-id>/\n    92\t```\n    93\t\n    94\tRecord task ID, worker/model, timestamps, context hash, token/cost usage if available, commits, tests, retries, errors, and disposition.\n    95\t\n    96\t## Budget Governance\n    97\t\n    98\tAdd project-level limits as well as ticket limits, e.g. daily budget, max concurrent workers, and pause thresholds for accumulated human-review items.\n    99\t\n   100\t## Human Intervention Queue\n   101\t\n   102\tQuestions should be small and concrete. Once the human makes an architecture/design decision, persist it so agents do not ask the same question repeatedly.\n   103\t\n   104\t## Long-Term Desired Experience\n   105\t\n   106\tThe user should be able to say:\n   107\t\n   108\t> Work through No Safe Circle's safe ready backlog until you need me.\n   109\t\n   110\tThen monitor GitHub to see what Claude is doing, what finished, what is blocked, what needs review, and what became ready next.\n   111\t\n   112\t## Definition of Success\n   113\t\n   114\t1. Project state survives chat/model restarts.\n   115\t2. Claude receives small bounded contexts.\n   116\t3. Dependencies are deterministic.\n   117\t4. Code is isolated by branch/worktree.\n   118\t5. Tests gate completion.\n   119\t6. Merge defines Done.\n   120\t7. Failures are bounded and observable.\n   121\t8. System moves to another ready task without human prompting.\n   122\t9. Roadmap changes are deliberate, not LLM drift.\n   123\t10. Token/cost use is much lower than repeated full-repository reasoning.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
