{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba 'Docs/AI-Pipeline/03_SUPERVISOR_GIT_GITHUB_CONTEXT.md'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Context 3 — Supervisor + Git Branches/Worktrees + GitHub Tickets/PRs\n     2\t\n     3\t## Goal\n     4\t\n     5\tCreate the first autonomous execution loop for **one ticket at a time**.\n     6\t\n     7\tPrerequisites: task graph, ready queue, and at least a minimal task context builder.\n     8\t\n     9\t## Critical Design Decision\n    10\t\n    11\tClaude does not own the autonomous loop. A local supervisor owns it and invokes Claude as a worker.\n    12\t\n    13\tThis allows project execution to resume after crashes, context loss, model session limits, and timeouts.\n    14\t\n    15\t## Git Strategy\n    16\t\n    17\tNever let autonomous workers modify `main` directly.\n    18\t\n    19\tFor a task such as NSC-014:\n    20\t\n    21\t```text\n    22\tbranch: claude/NSC-014-mana-resource\n    23\tworktree: .worktrees/NSC-014/\n    24\t```\n    25\t\n    26\tWorktrees isolate ticket work and prepare for future safe parallelism.\n    27\t\n    28\tDo **not** introduce parallel Claude workers yet.\n    29\t\n    30\t## GitHub Mapping\n    31\t\n    32\tEach local task should map to a GitHub Issue. GitHub is the human-facing dashboard.\n    33\t\n    34\tSuggested Project statuses:\n    35\t\n    36\t- Backlog\n    37\t- Ready\n    38\t- In Progress\n    39\t- Blocked\n    40\t- Validating\n    41\t- Needs Review\n    42\t- Done\n    43\t\n    44\tMirror task dependencies into GitHub when practical.\n    45\t\n    46\t## Source-of-Truth Split\n    47\t\n    48\tLocal task artifact owns durable definition: scope, dependencies, acceptance criteria, canon references.\n    49\t\n    50\tGitHub owns operational visibility: who/what is working, Draft PR, review state, blocked state, merge/close history.\n    51\t\n    52\tAvoid storing transient worker state in every Git branch.\n    53\t\n    54\t## Draft PR Early\n    55\t\n    56\tWhen a ticket is claimed:\n    57\t\n    58\t1. create branch/worktree\n    59\t2. mark GitHub Issue In Progress\n    60\t3. open Draft PR immediately\n    61\t4. launch Claude\n    62\t\n    63\tPR body should include ticket ID/title, scope, acceptance criteria, validation checklist, task-artifact reference, and a closing issue link/keyword when appropriate.\n    64\t\n    65\t## Commit Strategy\n    66\t\n    67\tClaude may make multiple working commits on its ticket branch, e.g.:\n    68\t\n    69\t```text\n    70\tNSC-014: Add PlayerMana component\n    71\tNSC-014: Add mana tests\n    72\tNSC-014: Fix regen delay behavior\n    73\t```\n    74\t\n    75\tEventually prefer squash merge into main so main contains one clean logical commit per completed ticket.\n    76\t\n    77\tA downstream dependency becomes satisfied only after the task is merged to main.\n    78\t\n    79\t## Supervisor First Version\n    80\t\n    81\t```text\n    82\t1. taskctl ready\n    83\t2. choose highest-ranked safe task\n    84\t3. claim it\n    85\t4. create branch/worktree\n    86\t5. open Draft PR\n    87\t6. build context\n    88\t7. run Claude\n    89\t8. collect result\n    90\t9. move to validation\n    91\t```\n    92\t\n    93\tDo not automate merge until validation is reliable.\n    94\t\n    95\t## Claims / Leases\n    96\t\n    97\tImplement a claim concept before parallelism:\n    98\t\n    99\t- task ID\n   100\t- worker ID\n   101\t- started time\n   102\t- expiration/heartbeat later\n   103\t\n   104\tTasks may eventually have conflict/resource claims, e.g. `System:PlayerResources` or `Scene:DoorPrototype`.\n   105\t\n   106\t## Failure Behavior\n   107\t\n   108\tIf Claude fails/times out:\n   109\t\n   110\t- preserve task, branch, PR, and logs\n   111\t- do not mark complete\n   112\t- retry only within configured limits\n   113\t- make supervisor restartable/idempotent\n   114\t\n   115\t## Completion Criteria\n   116\t\n   117\tOne real ticket can reliably go:\n   118\t\n   119\t```text\n   120\tReady → Claimed → Branch/Worktree → Draft PR → Claude implementation → commits visible → waiting for validation\n   121\t```\n   122\t\n   123\t## Next\n   124\t\n   125\tContinue with `04_EXECUTION_GER_VALIDATION_CONTEXT.md`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
