{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba Docs/AI-Pipeline/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '381,760p'\"","aggregated_output":"   381\t\n   382\t```text\n   383\tBASE-NSC-023-86af98f41ab5\n   384\t```\n   385\t\n   386\tThe production proof is bound to:\n   387\t\n   388\t- validated implementation commit: `86af98f41ab53016ef55eca9516cc339a1e4f5d1`;\n   389\t- validated implementation tree: `3e89c4a4879d1bf4179ae48f95b85dee1abc0d4d`;\n   390\t- evidence commit: `8933e67c7767abf45634f7bade79c734f334eea5`;\n   391\t- authoritative centralized scene: `Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity`;\n   392\t- scene meta GUID: `92dbd0a3e6c18e245896a66c5120379d`;\n   393\t- in-memory builder suite: 12 passed, 0 failed;\n   394\t- direct committed-scene camera suite: 2 passed, 0 failed;\n   395\t- Unity version for both runs: `6000.1.8f1`;\n   396\t- repository state after both runs: clean;\n   397\t- required human Play Mode approval: explicitly approved by Vincent Liguori.\n   398\t\n   399\tUncommitted evidence was correctly ignored before commit. Committing the evidence changed the derived state from `not_delivered` to `conformant`.\n   400\t\n   401\t### Phase 3A regression status\n   402\t\n   403\tThe conformance evaluator smoke test passes and proves, in a temporary Git repository, at least:\n   404\t\n   405\t1. no records -> `not_delivered`;\n   406\t2. valid committed delivery -> `conformant`;\n   407\t3. unrelated descendant commit with unchanged conformance surfaces -> still `conformant`;\n   408\t4. tracked implementation-surface change -> `needs_revalidation`;\n   409\t5. GDD change -> `needs_revalidation`;\n   410\t6. task-contract revision/hash change -> `needs_replan`;\n   411\t7. missing required human approval -> `needs_human`;\n   412\t8. malformed/missing gate, wrong tree/blob, or altered evidence artifact -> `invalid_evidence`;\n   413\t9. validated commit not ancestral to HEAD -> stale/revalidation-required state;\n   414\t10. valid revalidation after a tracked change -> `conformant`;\n   415\t11. incomparable current evidence -> `ambiguous_evidence`;\n   416\t12. uncommitted evidence is ignored because authority is committed HEAD.\n   417\t\n   418\tExisting TaskGraph transform, graph validation, persistence, taskcontrol, migration, quality-audit, and Phase 1 authorization regressions also pass.\n   419\t\n   420\tThe Python `py_compile` command is not used through `codex-review` because Python attempts to write `__pycache__` into the intentionally read-only repository mount. The actual smoke tests import and execute the new modules successfully.\n   421\t\n   422\t## Provider-Neutral Execution Crew Preparatory Stage 1 — COMPLETE\n   423\t\n   424\tStage 1 of `Docs/AI-Pipeline/06_PROVIDER_NEUTRAL_EXECUTION_CREW_PLAN.md` established the canonical provider-neutral Unity testing policy and deterministic clean runner before the Phase 3B proof.\n   425\t\n   426\tImplemented:\n   427\t\n   428\t- `Docs/Engineering/UNITY_TESTING_POLICY.md`;\n   429\t- the provider-neutral testing-policy instruction bridge in `AGENTS.md`;\n   430\t- the testing-policy import in `CLAUDE.md`;\n   431\t- `Pipeline/Testing/run_unity_tests_clean.ps1`;\n   432\t- `Pipeline/Testing/testing_policy_smoke_test.py`;\n   433\t- `Pipeline/Testing/README.md`.\n   434\t\n   435\tDeterministic checks passed:\n   436\t\n   437\t- `testing_policy_smoke_test.py`;\n   438\t- Windows PowerShell syntax parsing of `run_unity_tests_clean.ps1`.\n   439\t\n   440\tThe clean runner was also proven through a real Unity run with these exact facts:\n   441\t\n   442\t- branch: `phase-3-evidence-derived-conformance`;\n   443\t- commit: `1d3ed42db6fd595283bd1b57a008a4f4c5438796`;\n   444\t- tree: `9ce6f9fae545bc187f6b3869c4c36b17ac5f8a45`;\n   445\t- Unity: `6000.1.8f1`;\n   446\t- platform: `PlayMode`;\n   447\t- filter: `NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype.Tests.DoorInteractionPlayModeTests`;\n   448\t- total: 5;\n   449\t- passed: 5;\n   450\t- failed: 0;\n   451\t- skipped: 0;\n   452\t- result: `Passed`;\n   453\t- Unity exit code: 0;\n   454\t- repository clean before and after the run.\n   455\t\n   456\tThe runner proves Unity and Git execution facts. The separately committed NSC-023 baseline record binds those facts into Phase 3 conformance evidence. Neither the runner nor a conformant result enables readiness or authorization; `taskcontrol ready` remains unavailable and `taskcontrol authorize` remains denied.\n   457\t\n   458\tStage 1 itself did **not** implement `AgentRuntime`, provider adapters, `ExecutionCrew`, or a dedicated test-author agent. The provider-neutral `AgentRuntime` foundation was implemented later in Stage 3; live provider adapters and production `ExecutionCrew` roles remain later stages governed by the plan and ADR-034.\n   459\t\n   460\t## Provider-Neutral Execution Crew Stage 3 — COMPLETE\n   461\t\n   462\tStage 3 of `Docs/AI-Pipeline/06_PROVIDER_NEUTRAL_EXECUTION_CREW_PLAN.md` extracted the reusable orchestration concepts demonstrated by Assignment 3 into a new production foundation under:\n   463\t\n   464\t`Pipeline/AgentRuntime/`\n   465\t\n   466\tHistorical coursework remains preserved:\n   467\t\n   468\t- `AgentCrew/` remains Assignment 3 evidence and was not rewritten to use the new runtime;\n   469\t- `Assignment6GER/` remains Assignment 6 evidence and was not rewritten to use the new runtime.\n   470\t\n   471\tImplemented Stage 3 foundation files include:\n   472\t\n   473\t- `Pipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md`;\n   474\t- `Pipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py`;\n   475\t- `Pipeline/AgentRuntime/json_values.py`;\n   476\t- `Pipeline/AgentRuntime/schema_validation.py`;\n   477\t- `Pipeline/AgentRuntime/config.py`;\n   478\t- `Pipeline/AgentRuntime/agent_runner.py`;\n   479\t- `Pipeline/AgentRuntime/providers/base.py`;\n   480\t- `Pipeline/AgentRuntime/providers/fake.py`;\n   481\t- `Pipeline/AgentRuntime/tests/agent_runtime_smoke_test.py`;\n   482\t- `Pipeline/AgentRuntime/config/example.json`.\n   483\t\n   484\t### Stage 3 contract boundary\n   485\t\n   486\tStage 3 originally named its task-bound request `AgentRequest`. Stage 4B.3 replaces that production contract with generic `AgentInvocationRequest`; `TaskExecutionRequest` now owns NSC task identity above the runtime. `AgentResult` remains provider-neutral and schema 1.0.\n   487\t\n   488\tThe runtime distinguishes provider/agent **claims** from deterministic facts. In particular:\n   489\t\n   490\t- claimed changed paths do not replace Git diff/scope checks;\n   491\t- claimed test commands do not prove tests ran;\n   492\t- provider success does not prove Unity success;\n   493\t- provider output does not establish integrated delivery;\n   494\t- provider output does not establish current conformance;\n   495\t- provider output does not establish readiness or dispatch authorization.\n   496\t\n   497\t### Stage 3 runtime safety\n   498\t\n   499\tThe foundation now fail-closes on malformed or unsafe runtime data, including:\n   500\t\n   501\t- invalid task/contract identity;\n   502\t- unsafe repository-relative paths and Windows path aliases;\n   503\t- unsupported or missing capabilities;\n   504\t- invalid/excessive budgets;\n   505\t- malformed or cyclic JSON;\n   506\t- unsupported schema keywords;\n   507\t- mutable/polymorphic provider values crossing the trust boundary;\n   508\t- malformed raw logs or diagnostics;\n   509\t- schema-invalid structured output;\n   510\t- duplicate run identities;\n   511\t- attempts to overwrite finalized run artifacts.\n   512\t\n   513\tProvider failures are normalized into provider-neutral result classifications. Post-invocation schema failures preserve otherwise-valid non-authoritative audit claims and usage while rejecting the structured output itself.\n   514\t\n   515\tThe deterministic fake provider exercises success, provider failure, timeout, permission denial, budget exhaustion, schema failure, malformed metadata, and trust-boundary cases without network, shell, Git, Unity, or repository side effects.\n   516\t\n   517\t### Stage 3 regression status\n   518\t\n   519\tThe Stage 3 AgentRuntime smoke suite passes after adversarial hardening and covers the request/result contracts, configuration, provider registry, write boundaries, strict JSON/schema behavior, immutable publication, normalized failures, fake-provider scenarios, provider trust-boundary attacks, and protection of the historical Assignment 3 and Assignment 6 directories.\n   520\t\n   521\tStage 3 does **not** implement:\n   522\t\n   523\t- a live Claude Code provider;\n   524\t- a live OpenAI/Codex provider;\n   525\t- automatic provider fallback;\n   526\t- Implementer/Test Author/Validator orchestration;\n   527\t- Unity execution initiated by an agent;\n   528\t- GER integration;\n   529\t- task selection;\n   530\t- dependency readiness;\n   531\t- dispatch authorization;\n   532\t- automatic Git branch/worktree/commit/merge behavior.\n   533\t\n   534\t## Current Dispatch Policy\n   535\t\n   536\tEvidence-derived state inspection exists, but **dependency readiness and autonomous dispatch are not enabled**.\n   537\t\n   538\tCurrent readiness command:\n   539\t\n   540\t```powershell\n   541\tdocker compose run --rm codex-review python3 Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py ready\n   542\t```\n   543\t\n   544\tExpected output begins:\n   545\t\n   546\t```text\n   547\tTASK READINESS: UNAVAILABLE — DISPATCH POLICY NOT ENABLED\n   548\t```\n   549\t\n   550\tand explicitly states:\n   551\t\n   552\t- evidence-derived current-state inspection exists through `taskcontrol state`;\n   553\t- evidence-derived current conformance has been proven on at least one real task;\n   554\t- a conformant result does not establish dependency readiness;\n   555\t- dependency-readiness policy has not been implemented or approved;\n   556\t- dispatch authorization policy has not been implemented or approved;\n   557\t- state inspection and a conformant result never authorize autonomous execution;\n   558\t- zero tasks are authorized for autonomous dispatch.\n   559\t\n   560\tAuthorization command:\n   561\t\n   562\t```powershell\n   563\tdocker compose run --rm codex-review python3 Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py authorize NSC-023\n   564\t```\n   565\t\n   566\tExpected result:\n   567\t\n   568\t```text\n   569\tEXECUTION AUTHORIZATION: DENIED\n   570\treason_code: evidence_derived_dispatch_policy_not_enabled\n   571\t```\n   572\t\n   573\tA nonzero exit from `authorize` is an intentional policy denial, not a Docker failure.\n   574\t\n   575\t## Source-of-Truth Boundaries\n   576\t\n   577\t### Game-design canon\n   578\t\n   579\tThe current human-approved GDD and explicit approved design decisions define intended behavior.\n   580\t\n   581\t### Production GDD retrieval\n   582\t\n   583\t`Pipeline/GDDRAG` provides current, hash-bound, integrity-validated retrieval over the canonical GDD. It is not a substitute for complete canon when retrieval coverage has not been proven.\n   584\t\n   585\t### Task contracts\n   586\t\n   587\t`Tasks/*.yaml` defines approved work identity, scope, dependencies, acceptance criteria, completion gates, downstream obligations, exclusive resources, contract revision/disposition, and provenance.\n   588\t\n   589\tTask contracts do not contain current execution or completion truth.\n   590\t\n   591\t### Integrated implementation\n   592\t\n   593\tThe integrated Git tree is the authority for what code and assets are present.\n   594\t\n   595\tPresence alone is not completion proof.\n   596\t\n   597\t### Delivery/revalidation records\n   598\t\n   599\tPhase 3 records are immutable evidence claims tied to exact task, canon, Git, gate, artifact, and approval identities.\n   600\t\n   601\tA record does not contain mutable current-completion authority.\n   602\t\n   603\t### Current conformance\n   604\t\n   605\t`Pipeline/TaskGraph/current_conformance.py` deterministically evaluates committed evidence against current committed HEAD.\n   606\t\n   607\tState inspection is now implemented.\n   608\t\n   609\tProduction proof now exists for NSC-023 through committed baseline `BASE-NSC-023-86af98f41ab5`. No real production revalidation record exists yet.\n   610\t\n   611\t### AgentRuntime requests/results\n   612\t\n   613\t`Pipeline/AgentRuntime` is the provider-neutral execution boundary for future model invocations.\n   614\t\n   615\tIts immutable request, result, configuration, and provider-log artifacts are execution records and audit data. They are **not** game-design authority, deterministic validation evidence, current conformance, readiness, dispatch authorization, or human approval.\n   616\t\n   617\tProvider-reported changed paths, executed commands, tests, usage, and structured output remain claims until independently checked by the appropriate deterministic Git, Unity, schema, TaskGraph, or human process.\n   618\t\n   619\t### Reconciliation\n   620\t\n   621\tReconciliation outputs remain immutable point-in-time observations. They may propose graph changes but do not directly mutate living task contracts or current conformance state.\n   622\t\n   623\tRoutine GDD iteration should eventually use reviewed, scoped impact analysis rather than global reconciliation after every edit.\n   624\t\n   625\t### Architecture review evidence\n   626\t\n   627\tThe preserved architecture review is primary evidence for the accepted correction direction, but reviewer recommendations do not automatically become project decisions.\n   628\t\n   629\t## Immediate Next Goal\n   630\t\n   631\t### Migrate ArchitectureReview through generic AgentRuntime using Claude\n   632\t\n   633\tStage 4B.2 repository read/search and Stage 4B.3 responsibility separation are complete. `AgentInvocationRequest` schema 1.0 is generic; `TaskExecutionRequest` schema 1.0 separately owns NSC identity; `AgentResult` remains schema 1.0. `ProviderOutputInvalid` normalization is already implemented.\n   634\t\n   635\tThe next useful production proof is to migrate ArchitectureReview through AgentRuntime using the existing Claude adapter. That later slice should retain ArchitectureReview workflow identity above AgentRuntime and should not invent a task identity. The OpenAI/Codex provider remains unimplemented.\n   636\t\n   637\tCurrent provider budget policy remains:\n   638\t\n   639\t- Claude Code: native `--max-turns N` plus external `timeout_seconds`;\n   640\t- OpenAI/Codex: `effective_timeout_seconds = min(timeout_seconds, turn_limit * 30)` using the temporary 30-seconds-per-turn-budget-unit policy;\n   641\t- non-null `token_limit`: fail closed;\n   642\t- no automatic model/provider fallback.\n   643\t\n   644\tStage 4 must remain bounded:\n   645\t\n   646\t- no provider-specific task contracts or role schemas;\n   647\t- no automatic provider fallback that changes task meaning;\n   648\t- no production `ExecutionCrew` role orchestration yet;\n   649\t- no real gameplay task execution yet;\n   650\t- no Unity validation delegated to a model;\n   651\t- no Phase 3 evidence publication by an adapter;\n   652\t- no dependency readiness;\n   653\t- no dispatch authorization;\n   654\t- no automatic merge.\n   655\t\n   656\tArchitecture Correction Phase 3 authority remains active:\n   657\t\n   658\t- `NSC-023` derives as `conformant`;\n   659\t- readiness remains unavailable;\n   660\t- authorization remains denied;\n   661\t- no worker, provider, runtime, or future adapter result establishes completion, readiness, or dispatch authority.\n   662\t\n   663\tNo real production revalidation record exists yet. Do not fabricate a gameplay, contract, GDD, scene, implementation, or test change merely to produce one. The first legitimate relevant change will exercise the production revalidation path.\n   664\t\n   665\t## Real Gameplay Task Selection After the Evidence Proof\n   666\t\n   667\tThe first gameplay implementation task is **not automatically selected** by this document, the graph, or reviewer consensus.\n   668\t\n   669\t`NSC-037` was discussed during architecture review as a possible delivery-lane experiment. It is not the committed gameplay priority.\n   670\t\n   671\t`NSC-003` remains a possible high-leverage gameplay anchor, but it should not be handed to a worker unchanged merely because its task contract currently says `single_agent`.\n   672\t\n   673\tBefore implementing NSC-003, human review should resolve:\n   674\t\n   675\t- which Input Action owns click-to-move/select;\n   676\t- arbitration among UI click, movement, Fireball, Frost Field, Force Wave, and door selection;\n   677\t- click versus held-pointer steering;\n   678\t- destination replacement and cancellation;\n   679\t- approach/arrival semantics;\n   680\t- movement pathing expectations;\n   681\t- movement-restriction ownership/release semantics.\n   682\t\n   683\tHuman review should also decide whether NSC-003 should be superseded by smaller contracts, for example:\n   684\t\n   685\t- runtime input and shared pointer-projection foundation;\n   686\t- mouse-directed movement, restriction, reset, and suspension.\n   687\t\n   688\t## Deferred Until Evidence Justifies It\n   689\t\n   690\tDo not enable or build these merely because Phase 3 exists:\n   691\t\n   692\t- dependency-derived `taskcontrol ready`;\n   693\t- autonomous execution authorization;\n   694\t- autonomous task claiming or continuous dispatch;\n   695\t- parallel workers or broad worktree orchestration;\n   696\t- automatic merge/merge queues;\n   697\t- broad GitHub Issues/Projects synchronization;\n   698\t- automatic backlog replenishment;\n   699\t- full-game speculative decomposition;\n   700\t- Progressive Decomposer as a bundled platform;\n   701\t- Artifact Authority without a real blocking design need;\n   702\t- top-k-only task context presented as complete canon;\n   703\t- automatic GDD impact analysis without a reviewed causal model;\n   704\t- a general supervisor before repeated delivery bottlenecks justify one.\n   705\t\n   706\tThese remain later candidates driven by observed production needs rather than roadmap momentum.\n   707\t\n   708\t## Obsolete Branch/Plan Warning\n   709\t\n   710\tDo not resume `milestone-2a-nsc-003-context` unchanged.\n   711\t\n   712\tThat branch predates the accepted architecture corrections, task-contract schema 2.0, reviewed migration corrections, production GDD RAG integrity boundary, and Phase 3 conformance model.\n   713\t\n   714\tUseful ideas should be recreated from the corrected current repository state rather than continuing the obsolete plan as written.\n   715\t\n   716\t## Next Window Instructions\n   717\t\n   718\tRead, in order:\n   719\t\n   720\t1. `Docs/AI-Pipeline/START_HERE.md`;\n   721\t2. this file;\n   722\t3. `Docs/AI-Pipeline/00_MASTER_CONTEXT.md`;\n   723\t4. `Docs/AI-Pipeline/DECISIONS.md`;\n   724\t5. `Docs/AI-Pipeline/06_PROVIDER_NEUTRAL_EXECUTION_CREW_PLAN.md`;\n   725\t6. `Docs/AI-Pipeline/ADR-034_PROVIDER_NEUTRAL_AGENT_RUNTIME.md`;\n   726\t7. `Docs/AI-Pipeline/07_PROVIDER_ADAPTER_CAPABILITY_MAPPING.md`;\n   727\t8. `Docs/AI-Pipeline/ADR-035_PROVIDER_ADAPTER_ENFORCEMENT.md`;\n   728\t9. `Pipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md`;\n   729\t10. `Pipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py`;\n   730\t11. `Pipeline/AgentRuntime/agent_runner.py`;\n   731\t12. `Pipeline/AgentRuntime/providers/base.py`;\n   732\t13. `Pipeline/AgentRuntime/tests/agent_runtime_smoke_test.py`;\n   733\t14. inspect the actual repository and branch state.\n   734\t\n   735\tThen:\n   736\t\n   737\t1. confirm the intended `provider-adapters` branch and inspect the working tree without discarding existing changes;\n   738\t2. confirm ADR-035 remains recorded as accepted/amended and ADR-036 records the transport ownership decision;\n   739\t3. read ADR-039 and inspect `Pipeline/TaskExecution` before adding any task-associated consumer;\n   740\t4. migrate ArchitectureReview through generic AgentRuntime using Claude in the next reviewed slice; do not implement the OpenAI/Codex provider as part of that migration;\n   741\t5. use only opt-in, non-production-write live smoke tests during Stage 4;\n   742\t6. do not implement production `ExecutionCrew` roles until both adapters pass the shared fixture suite;\n   743\t7. keep `taskcontrol ready` unavailable and `taskcontrol authorize` denied.\n   744\t\n   745\tA new window should be able to resume from repository state without the prior chat transcript.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
