{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba Docs/AI-Pipeline/00_MASTER_CONTEXT.md | sed -n '1,330p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# No Safe Circle — Autonomous AI Development Pipeline\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\t## Master Context / Architecture Handoff\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\tUse this file for the durable target architecture when continuing work on the autonomous development pipeline.\r\n     6\t\r\n     7\tFor exact current implementation status, always read `CURRENT_STATE.md` first.\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\tLast architecture/status reconciliation: 2026-08-21, after Milestone 1 completion and the post-M1 adversarial-architecture-review branch merge.\r\n    10\t\r\n    11\t## Current Architecture Status\r\n    12\t\r\n    13\tThe architecture is no longer purely prospective.\r\n    14\t\r\n    15\t**Milestone 1 is implemented and merged.** The repository now contains:\r\n    16\t\r\n    17\t- a human-approved persistent work graph under `Tasks/`;\r\n    18\t- stable `NSC-###` work IDs;\r\n    19\t- reconciliation-key provenance;\r\n    20\t- deterministic graph validation;\r\n    21\t- deterministic dependency/parent hierarchy reconstruction;\r\n    22\t- exclusive-resource metadata;\r\n    23\t- project-level non-code requirements;\r\n    24\t- a working local `taskcontrol` CLI;\r\n    25\t- a real deterministic ready frontier.\r\n    26\t\r\n    27\tThe current graph contains 37 work records and the first real `taskcontrol ready` calculation returned seven executable one-agent implementation tasks.\r\n    28\t\r\n    29\tThe next planned infrastructure milestone is Milestone 2: targeted GDD/project context, Progressive Decomposition, and Artifact Authority.\r\n    30\t\r\n    31\tBefore substantial Milestone 2 expansion, the M1-complete architecture should be reviewed through `Pipeline/ArchitectureReview/` and any accepted architectural corrections should be persisted in `DECISIONS.md` and `CURRENT_STATE.md`.\r\n    32\t\r\n    33\t## Project\r\n    34\t\r\n    35\tRepository: `https://github.com/cathode26/NoSafeCircle`\r\n    36\t\r\n    37\tCourse work already provides reusable building blocks:\r\n    38\t\r\n    39\t- Assignment 3: Agent Crew concept — Planner → Implementer → Validator.\r\n    40\t- Assignment 4: RAG/retrieval over the No Safe Circle GDD.\r\n    41\t- Assignment 5: goal-oriented gap analysis and bounded implementation agent.\r\n    42\t- Assignment 6: working GER implementation — Implement/Generate → Evaluate → Refine → Circuit Breaker, including runtime-feedback repair.\r\n    43\t- Assignment 7: not yet implemented; intended to become a scored Style Evaluator specialization when real authorized style-sensitive artifact work exists.\r\n    44\t\r\n    45\tThe production goal is to evolve these pieces into a system that can continue developing No Safe Circle while keeping project state durable, observable, resumable after model/context failures, bounded in cost, grounded in real Unity evidence, and protected from silent AI invention of missing game design.\r\n    46\t\r\n    47\t## Core Architectural Decision\r\n    48\t\r\n    49\tThe LLM does **not** own durable project state or the continuous autonomous loop.\r\n    50\t\r\n    51\tA local deterministic supervisor eventually owns the loop.\r\n    52\t\r\n    53\tClaude or another coding model is a bounded worker that receives one small piece of approved work at a time.\r\n    54\t\r\n    55\tPersistent project state lives in repository artifacts and later GitHub operational state, not in a model context window.\r\n    56\t\r\n    57\tA worker may implement or generate work, but it does not declare that work complete. Completion is determined by project evidence plus merge/approval state.\r\n    58\t\r\n    59\tAn implementation worker also does not silently invent missing game design. Missing design becomes an explicit artifact proposal.\r\n    60\t\r\n    61\t## Desired End-to-End Loop\r\n    62\t\r\n    63\t```text\r\n    64\tGDD / Root Canon\r\n    65\t ↓\r\n    66\tPersistent Work Graph                         ← M1 COMPLETE\r\n    67\t ↓\r\n    68\tReady / Near-Ready Frontier                   ← M1 COMPLETE\r\n    69\t ↓\r\n    70\tTargeted Task + GDD + Project Context          ← M2 NEXT\r\n    71\t ↓\r\n    72\tProgressive Decomposer\r\n    73\t ↓\r\n    74\tEnough approved information?\r\n    75\t ├─ yes → Concrete child work\r\n    76\t └─ no  → Proposed artifact\r\n    77\t               ↓\r\n    78\t         Artifact Authority Gate\r\n    79\t               ↓\r\n    80\t          Authorized?\r\n    81\t          /       \\\r\n    82\t        yes        no\r\n    83\t         ↓          ↓\r\n    84\t   Artifact Generator   Re-plan / Human Review\r\n    85\t         ↓\r\n    86\t      Artifact GER\r\n    87\t         ├─ Canon / Design Evaluator\r\n    88\t         ├─ Completeness Evaluator\r\n    89\t         └─ Style Evaluator when applicable\r\n    90\t         ↓\r\n    91\t   Approved Artifact\r\n    92\t         ↓\r\n    93\t   Back to Decomposer\r\n    94\t         ↓\r\n    95\t   Concrete Work Item\r\n    96\t         ↓\r\n    97\tLocal Supervisor                               ← M3\r\n    98\t ↓\r\n    99\tClaim Ticket\r\n   100\t ↓\r\n   101\tGit Branch + Git Worktree + Draft PR\r\n   102\t ↓\r\n   103\tBuild Small Context Package\r\n   104\t ↓\r\n   105\tBounded Worker / Agent Crew\r\n   106\t ↓\r\n   107\t==============================\r\n   108\t        GER EXECUTION LOOP                     ← M4 production integration\r\n   109\t------------------------------\r\n   110\tImplement / Generate\r\n   111\t ↓\r\n   112\tTask/GDD/Artifact Evaluation\r\n   113\t ↓\r\n   114\tDeterministic Validation\r\n   115\t ↓\r\n   116\tUnity / Runtime Validation\r\n   117\t ↓\r\n   118\tPASS?\r\n   119\t ├─ yes → Approved Work\r\n   120\t └─ no  → Feedback Bundle → Refiner → Re-evaluate\r\n   121\t                         ↓\r\n   122\t                 retry/cost/runtime limit\r\n   123\t                         ↓\r\n   124\t                  Circuit Breaker\r\n   125\t==============================\r\n   126\t ↓\r\n   127\tFresh AI Diff Review\r\n   128\t ↓\r\n   129\tPR Merge / Artifact Approval\r\n   130\t ↓\r\n   131\tWork = Complete\r\n   132\t ↓\r\n   133\tDependency Graph Recalculates\r\n   134\t ↓\r\n   135\tNew Work Becomes Ready\r\n   136\t ↓\r\n   137\tContinuous Safe Backlog Processing             ← M5\r\n   138\t```\r\n   139\t\r\n   140\tThe exact evaluator order may vary by work type, but cheap deterministic failures should be detected before spending model tokens on semantic review whenever practical.\r\n   141\t\r\n   142\t## Guiding Principle\r\n   143\t\r\n   144\t**Use deterministic code for facts and computation. Use LLMs for semantic judgment and bounded implementation.**\r\n   145\t\r\n   146\tDeterministic/local responsibilities include:\r\n   147\t\r\n   148\t- work identity and dependency bookkeeping;\r\n   149\t- graph validation/readiness;\r\n   150\t- file enumeration;\r\n   151\t- code/component detection;\r\n   152\t- Unity YAML inspection;\r\n   153\t- `.meta` GUID relationships;\r\n   154\t- obvious project-state queries;\r\n   155\t- Git/scope checks;\r\n   156\t- compilation/test orchestration;\r\n   157\t- progress/no-op detection;\r\n   158\t- budget/circuit-breaker bookkeeping.\r\n   159\t\r\n   160\tLLM responsibilities include:\r\n   161\t\r\n   162\t- semantic decomposition of bounded near-frontier work;\r\n   163\t- deciding whether approved information is sufficient to decompose;\r\n   164\t- distinguishing missing design from oversized implementation scope;\r\n   165\t- interpreting genuinely ambiguous intent;\r\n   166\t- bounded implementation planning/coding;\r\n   167\t- semantic task/GDD evaluation;\r\n   168\t- fresh semantic diff review;\r\n   169\t- authorized design/content generation;\r\n   170\t- style evaluation/refinement;\r\n   171\t- repair from structured failure evidence.\r\n   172\t\r\n   173\t## Sources of Truth\r\n   174\t\r\n   175\t### Root Canon\r\n   176\t\r\n   177\tThe current GDD is root game-design canon.\r\n   178\t\r\n   179\tRAG should retrieve only relevant canonical chunks instead of repeatedly sending the entire GDD to a model.\r\n   180\t\r\n   181\tPrior assignment artifacts may provide history or reusable machinery, but they do not override current GDD or integrated repository state.\r\n   182\t\r\n   183\t### Approved Design Extensions\r\n   184\t\r\n   185\tApproved artifact outputs may later extend root canon with project-authorized detail.\r\n   186\t\r\n   187\tAn artifact becomes trusted only after this path:\r\n   188\t\r\n   189\t```text\r\n   190\tArtifact proposal\r\n   191\t ↓\r\n   192\tArtifact Authority Gate\r\n   193\t ↓\r\n   194\tAuthorized generation\r\n   195\t ↓\r\n   196\tRequired evaluators / GER\r\n   197\t ↓\r\n   198\tApproved artifact\r\n   199\t ↓\r\n   200\tTrusted downstream input\r\n   201\t```\r\n   202\t\r\n   203\tApproved artifacts may add detail only inside the authority granted to them. They may not contradict or silently replace GDD canon.\r\n   204\t\r\n   205\tUnapproved drafts are not trusted design input.\r\n   206\t\r\n   207\t### Codebase Truth\r\n   208\t\r\n   209\tThe current integrated `main` branch is the authority for what implementation actually exists and is complete.\r\n   210\t\r\n   211\tOld assignment planning output is not current codebase truth unless reconciled against the repository.\r\n   212\t\r\n   213\t### Durable Work Definition\r\n   214\t\r\n   215\tThe living operational work graph now exists under:\r\n   216\t\r\n   217\t```text\r\n   218\tTasks/\r\n   219\t  NSC-001.yaml\r\n   220\t  ...\r\n   221\t  NSC-037.yaml\r\n   222\t```\r\n   223\t\r\n   224\tInitial supported work kinds are:\r\n   225\t\r\n   226\t```text\r\n   227\tfeature\r\n   228\tartifact\r\n   229\timplementation\r\n   230\t```\r\n   231\t\r\n   232\tDefinitions:\r\n   233\t\r\n   234\t- `feature` — organizational/high-level work that may require progressive decomposition; never a direct implementation handoff.\r\n   235\t- `artifact` — work whose output is approved design/content; complete only after required authority/evaluation/promotion.\r\n   236\t- `implementation` — concrete repository work that can be executed when dependencies and execution scope allow it.\r\n   237\t\r\n   238\tStable `reconciliation_key` values preserve traceability back to the reconciliation record that proposed each initial work item.\r\n   239\t\r\n   240\t### Operational Status\r\n   241\t\r\n   242\tDurable task definitions currently use `open` / `complete`.\r\n   243\t\r\n   244\tLater, GitHub Issues/Projects should provide human-facing transient execution visibility such as:\r\n   245\t\r\n   246\t- Backlog\r\n   247\t- Ready\r\n   248\t- In Progress\r\n   249\t- Blocked\r\n   250\t- Validating\r\n   251\t- Needs Review\r\n   252\t- Done\r\n   253\t\r\n   254\tDo not make ephemeral “worker is running” state a constantly committed task-file concern if the supervisor/GitHub can own it safely.\r\n   255\t\r\n   256\t## Milestone 1 Persistent Work Graph\r\n   257\t\r\n   258\tMilestone 1 is complete. See `01_MILESTONE_TASK_GRAPH.md` for its completion record.\r\n   259\t\r\n   260\tThe initial graph was created through:\r\n   261\t\r\n   262\t```text\r\n   263\tGDD + repository state\r\n   264\t ↓\r\n   265\timmutable reconciliation snapshot\r\n   266\t ↓\r\n   267\tindependent multi-model verification\r\n   268\t ↓\r\n   269\tbounded repair / re-verification\r\n   270\t ↓\r\n   271\t0 final material findings\r\n   272\t ↓\r\n   273\thuman approval\r\n   274\t ↓\r\n   275\tdeterministic bootstrap\r\n   276\t ↓\r\n   277\tpersistent graph\r\n   278\t```\r\n   279\t\r\n   280\tApproved reconciliation:\r\n   281\t\r\n   282\t`20260821T193541Z-998ee7b5`\r\n   283\t\r\n   284\tSuccessful verification:\r\n   285\t\r\n   286\t`20260821T195959Z-43dba5de`\r\n   287\t\r\n   288\tThe one-time bootstrap is marked by:\r\n   289\t\r\n   290\t`Pipeline/TaskGraph/BOOTSTRAP_PERSISTED.json`\r\n   291\t\r\n   292\tDo not rerun the initial `--apply` bootstrap after that marker exists.\r\n   293\t\r\n   294\t### Current Task-Control Interface\r\n   295\t\r\n   296\t```text\r\n   297\tpython Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py validate\r\n   298\tpython Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py list\r\n   299\tpython Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py show NSC-003\r\n   300\tpython Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py ready\r\n   301\tpython Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py graph\r\n   302\t```\r\n   303\t\r\n   304\tA work item is executable-ready only when it is open, is an `artifact` or `implementation`, has `execution_scope: single_agent`, and all dependencies are complete.\r\n   305\t\r\n   306\tThis readiness calculation is deterministic.\r\n   307\t\r\n   308\t## Reconciliation Boundary\r\n   309\t\r\n   310\tReconciliation is an immutable point-in-time observation, not the mutable work database.\r\n   311\t\r\n   312\tEvery full reconciliation run creates a new versioned snapshot of GDD requirements versus repository state.\r\n   313\t\r\n   314\tA later reconciliation may propose additions/changes/conflicts against the persistent graph, but the Reconciliation Agent does not directly rewrite `Tasks/*.yaml`.\r\n   315\t\r\n   316\tFuture graph changes must cross an explicit deterministic diff/review/apply boundary.\r\n   317\t\r\n   318\tOld reconciliation snapshots remain historically true even after later implementation changes the repository.\r\n   319\t\r\n   320\tThe persistent graph is the living operational state.\r\n   321\t\r\n   322\t## Progressive Task Decomposition\r\n   323\t\r\n   324\tThe graph should **not** contain the entire game's lowest-level implementation plan in advance.\r\n   325\t\r\n   326\tHigh-level work is decomposed just in time as it approaches the actionable frontier.\r\n   327\t\r\n   328\tThe Progressive Decomposer must first determine *why* an item is not a safe one-agent handoff.\r\n   329\t\r\n   330\tTwo distinct cases exist:\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
