{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba Docs/AI-Pipeline/00_MASTER_CONTEXT.md | sed -n '409,630p'\"","aggregated_output":"   409\t## Assignment 6 / GER Integration\r\n   410\t\r\n   411\tAssignment 6 proved the central repair-loop concept needed later for production execution:\r\n   412\t\r\n   413\t```text\r\n   414\tImplement / Generate\r\n   415\t ↓\r\n   416\tEvaluate\r\n   417\t ↓\r\n   418\tValidation Evidence\r\n   419\t ├─ PASS → approved\r\n   420\t └─ FAIL → structured feedback → Refiner → re-evaluate\r\n   421\t                                      ↓\r\n   422\t                               retry to budget\r\n   423\t                                      ↓\r\n   424\t                               Circuit Breaker\r\n   425\t```\r\n   426\t\r\n   427\tThe camera run established production rules:\r\n   428\t\r\n   429\t1. Static evaluator PASS is not sufficient for interactive Unity behavior.\r\n   430\t2. Runtime observations must re-enter the repair loop as structured evidence.\r\n   431\t3. Validation history should be auditable enough to reconstruct what happened.\r\n   432\t4. A Refiner that makes no relevant change while failures remain has not made progress.\r\n   433\t5. No-op repair attempts count against the repair budget.\r\n   434\t6. Circuit Breakers bound retries and escalate instead of looping forever.\r\n   435\t7. Evaluator contracts should be task/GDD specific, not merely “does it compile?”\r\n   436\t\r\n   437\tReference:\r\n   438\t\r\n   439\t`Assignment6GER/README_Assignment6.md`\r\n   440\t\r\n   441\t## Validation Evidence Model\r\n   442\t\r\n   443\tProduction execution should build an evidence bundle rather than trust one PASS/FAIL source.\r\n   444\t\r\n   445\tPossible evidence sources include:\r\n   446\t\r\n   447\t```text\r\n   448\tGit / scope validation\r\n   449\tStatic checks\r\n   450\tUnity compilation\r\n   451\tEditMode tests\r\n   452\tPlayMode tests\r\n   453\tRuntime observations\r\n   454\tSimulation/adversarial-agent results (later)\r\n   455\tTask/GDD semantic evaluation\r\n   456\tArtifact canon/design evaluation\r\n   457\tArtifact completeness evaluation\r\n   458\tStyle evaluation when applicable\r\n   459\tFresh semantic diff review\r\n   460\t```\r\n   461\t\r\n   462\tNot every work item needs every evaluator.\r\n   463\t\r\n   464\tWork type, source requirements, acceptance criteria, and risk determine which evidence is required.\r\n   465\t\r\n   466\tFailures should be normalized into structured Refiner input.\r\n   467\t\r\n   468\t## Assignment 7 / Style Evaluator Integration\r\n   469\t\r\n   470\tAssignment 7 should not become a parallel autonomous architecture.\r\n   471\t\r\n   472\tWhen Progressive Decomposition identifies an authorized style-sensitive artifact, Assignment 7 can supply a scored evaluator inside Artifact GER:\r\n   473\t\r\n   474\t```text\r\n   475\tGenerator\r\n   476\t ↓\r\n   477\tStyle Evaluator\r\n   478\t ↓\r\n   479\tSCORE + REASON\r\n   480\t ↓\r\n   481\tRefiner\r\n   482\t ↓\r\n   483\tStyle Evaluator\r\n   484\t```\r\n   485\t\r\n   486\tThe Style Evaluator judges quality/style of content already authorized to exist.\r\n   487\t\r\n   488\tIt does not authorize creation of new canon or design content.\r\n   489\t\r\n   490\tArtifact authority and artifact quality remain separate decisions.\r\n   491\t\r\n   492\t## Git Model\r\n   493\t\r\n   494\tAutonomous implementation workers must not develop directly on `main`.\r\n   495\t\r\n   496\tFor each implementation ticket, Milestone 3 should eventually create a branch and worktree such as:\r\n   497\t\r\n   498\t```text\r\n   499\tbranch: claude/NSC-003-player-movement\r\n   500\tworktree: .worktrees/NSC-003/\r\n   501\t```\r\n   502\t\r\n   503\tExpected lifecycle:\r\n   504\t\r\n   505\t```text\r\n   506\tReady → Claimed → In Progress → Validating → PR Ready → Merged → Done\r\n   507\t```\r\n   508\t\r\n   509\t“Done” means merged/integrated evidence supports completion, not merely that a worker says it finished.\r\n   510\t\r\n   511\tDraft PRs should be opened early so humans can inspect ongoing work.\r\n   512\t\r\n   513\t## Autonomous Supervisor\r\n   514\t\r\n   515\tThe supervisor, not the model, owns the eventual continuous loop.\r\n   516\t\r\n   517\tConceptually:\r\n   518\t\r\n   519\t```python\r\n   520\twhile game_not_complete:\r\n   521\t    ready = taskcontrol.ready()\r\n   522\t\r\n   523\t    if not ready:\r\n   524\t        expand_near_frontier_or_reconcile()\r\n   525\t        continue\r\n   526\t\r\n   527\t    work = choose_safe_ready_work(ready)\r\n   528\t\r\n   529\t    if work_needs_decomposition(work):\r\n   530\t        run_progressive_decomposition(work)\r\n   531\t        continue\r\n   532\t\r\n   533\t    if work.kind == \"artifact\":\r\n   534\t        authorize_generate_evaluate_or_escalate(work)\r\n   535\t        continue\r\n   536\t\r\n   537\t    claim(work)\r\n   538\t    create_branch_worktree_and_draft_pr(work)\r\n   539\t    context = build_compact_context(work)\r\n   540\t    result = run_bounded_execution_ger(work, context)\r\n   541\t\r\n   542\t    if result.needs_human:\r\n   543\t        preserve_and_escalate(work)\r\n   544\t        continue\r\n   545\t\r\n   546\t    if validation_and_review_pass(result):\r\n   547\t        merge(work)\r\n   548\t        mark_complete(work)\r\n   549\t```\r\n   550\t\r\n   551\tThis remains target architecture; the supervisor itself is not yet implemented.\r\n   552\t\r\n   553\t## Safety / Cost Controls\r\n   554\t\r\n   555\tPer-work limits should eventually include:\r\n   556\t\r\n   557\t- maximum agent runs;\r\n   558\t- maximum repair attempts;\r\n   559\t- maximum runtime;\r\n   560\t- model/token budget;\r\n   561\t- maximum no-progress attempts.\r\n   562\t\r\n   563\tStop/escalate for:\r\n   564\t\r\n   565\t- repeated validation failure;\r\n   566\t- GDD ambiguity;\r\n   567\t- unauthorized design expansion;\r\n   568\t- architecture-changing dependencies;\r\n   569\t- Unity scene/prefab/shared-resource conflict;\r\n   570\t- scope expansion;\r\n   571\t- budget exhaustion;\r\n   572\t- repeated no-op refinement.\r\n   573\t\r\n   574\tAutonomous means “continue safe bounded work,” not “spend forever” or “invent whatever is missing.”\r\n   575\t\r\n   576\t## Parallelism\r\n   577\t\r\n   578\tDo not start with multiple coding workers.\r\n   579\t\r\n   580\tFirst make one-ticket execution reliable and restartable.\r\n   581\t\r\n   582\tLater parallelism must honor exclusive-resource claims and be conservative around Unity scenes, prefabs, ProjectSettings, Input Actions, and shared builder scripts.\r\n   583\t\r\n   584\t## Near-Term Build Strategy\r\n   585\t\r\n   586\tMilestone 1 is finished. Do not rebuild it.\r\n   587\t\r\n   588\tThe current strategy is:\r\n   589\t\r\n   590\t1. confirm `taskcontrol validate` and `taskcontrol ready` remain truthful;\r\n   591\t2. run/review the post-M1 adversarial architecture checkpoint;\r\n   592\t3. use one real ready/near-ready No Safe Circle task as the anchor for the next slice;\r\n   593\t4. build the smallest targeted task-context path needed for that work;\r\n   594\t5. reuse Assignment 4 RAG and existing deterministic reconciliation/scanner capabilities where practical;\r\n   595\t6. add Progressive Decomposition only when a near-frontier item actually needs it;\r\n   596\t7. create artifact proposals rather than invent missing design;\r\n   597\t8. authorize/evaluate generated artifacts before downstream use;\r\n   598\t9. add the single-ticket supervisor only after compact task context is reliable;\r\n   599\t10. productionize generic GER/Unity validation around real tickets;\r\n   600\t11. enable continuous autonomous backlog processing only after single-ticket execution is trustworthy;\r\n   601\t12. add parallel workers last.\r\n   602\t\r\n   603\tA strong current real-task anchor is `NSC-003` Player Movement because it is already ready, bounded, and unlocks multiple later systems.\r\n   604\t\r\n   605\tThis keeps pipeline development tied to capstone progress.\r\n   606\t\r\n   607\t## High-Level Build Milestones\r\n   608\t\r\n   609\t1. **Persistent work artifacts + deterministic `taskcontrol` — COMPLETE**\r\n   610\t2. **RAG canon service + deterministic project scanner + compact context builder + Progressive Decomposer + Artifact Authority Gate — NEXT**\r\n   611\t3. One-ticket autonomous supervisor with claims + branch/worktree/Draft PR\r\n   612\t4. Productionize GER execution + deterministic/Unity/runtime validation + evaluator profiles\r\n   613\t5. Continuous scheduling + blocker handling + budgets + GitHub visibility + eventual safe parallelism\r\n   614\t\r\n   615\tAssignment 6 has already produced a working prototype of Milestone 4's central repair-loop concept, so Milestone 4 is production integration rather than invention from zero.\r\n   616\t\r\n   617\t## Working Rule\r\n   618\t\r\n   619\tBuild in small stages.\r\n   620\t\r\n   621\tDo not try to implement the full autonomous pipeline in one context or coding session.\r\n   622\t\r\n   623\tEach meaningful session should leave durable repository state/documentation so the next session can resume without the previous chat transcript.\r\n   624\t\r\n   625\tFrom Milestone 2 onward, infrastructure should increasingly be proven by advancing actual No Safe Circle gameplay rather than becoming a separate project that indefinitely delays the game.\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
