{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'rg -n -C 3 \"repository_write|approved_command_execution|write_policy|WriteBoundaries|ProviderRequestRejected\" Pipeline/AgentRuntime/providers/openai_codex.py Pipeline/AgentRuntime/providers/claude_code.py Pipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py Pipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md'","aggregated_output":"Pipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md-4-\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md-5-`AgentInvocationRequest` describes one generic bounded invocation: run identity, role, prompt, repository context, semantic capabilities, write policy, output shape, capability-class selection, budgets, and provider configuration. It has no No Safe Circle task identity and no dependency on `Tasks/*.yaml`. `AgentResult` describes only an invocation outcome and provider/agent claims. Task identity belongs to `Pipeline/TaskExecution`; delivery, conformance, readiness, authorization, integration, repository changes, command execution, and test success remain decisions for higher deterministic repository, test, and evidence systems.\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md-6-\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md:7:All retained request, result, and runtime-configuration JSON values are recursively validated and frozen. Runtime configuration invariants apply equally to direct construction, dictionaries, and strict JSON loading. Only exact built-in JSON null, booleans, integers, finite numbers, valid UTF-8 strings, lists/tuples, dictionaries, and the runtime's own frozen mapping proxies are accepted. Polymorphic container and text subclasses are rejected so provider callbacks cannot run during validation or make publication disagree with the validated snapshot. Cycles and nesting deeper than the conservative 64-container limit are rejected deterministically. `to_dict()` methods return detached mutable copies. The runner accepts only the exact `AgentInvocationRequest`, `RuntimeConfiguration`, and `ProviderInvocationResponse` types; requests additionally require exact `WriteBoundaries` and `Budgets`, while results require exact `Usage`. Base serializers are called non-polymorphically, preventing subclass serialization or response-container overrides at these trust boundaries.\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md-8-\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md-9-Identifiers use conservative lowercase ASCII forms: run IDs are 1–64 character lowercase alphanumeric/hyphen slugs, while roles and configuration keys begin with a lowercase letter and use lowercase letters, digits, underscores, and separated hyphens. Every serialized operational string must be UTF-8 encodable. Repository paths are already-normalized, relative POSIX paths and additionally reject surrogates, NUL, ASCII controls, DEL, line breaks, tabs, Windows-forbidden characters, alternate-data-stream colons, trailing dots/spaces, and reserved Windows device names. Write-boundary components are compared conservatively and case-insensitively while remaining component-aware; denied boundaries override allowed ones. Budget maxima are 1,000 turns, 86,400 seconds, and 10,000,000 tokens.\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md-10-\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md-11-Provider adapters expose an identifier, accept the common request plus a configured concrete model, return structured output and raw log text separately, and normalize provider failures. They translate invocation mechanics only. They may never write task/evidence/readiness state or declare delivery, conformance, readiness, or authorization. Live-provider adapters must pass the same contract suite.\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md-12-\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md:13:`ProviderOutputInvalid` represents provider output from which an adapter could not produce a structured-output candidate. `AgentRunner` normalizes it to `schema_error`. This is distinct from a successfully parsed candidate that the runner later rejects through central schema validation, although both outcomes normalize to `schema_error`. `ProviderRequestRejected` represents a provider that cannot safely honor a selected request policy and normalizes to `invalid_request` after provider/model selection. Exact provider raw output is retained in `provider.log` when it is valid. Neither exception establishes deterministic correctness, delivery, conformance, readiness, authorization, approval, integration, or test-success authority.\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md-14-\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md-15-`FakeProvider` is deterministic and performs no network, command, version-control, engine, or repository access. It exercises success, provider failure, invalid provider output, timeout, permission denial, budget exhaustion, and centrally detected schema failure.\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md-16-\n--\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-18-    {\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-19-        \"repository_read\",\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-20-        \"repository_search\",\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py:21:        \"repository_write\",\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py:22:        \"approved_command_execution\",\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-23-    }\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-24-)\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-25-RESULT_STATUSES = frozenset({\"succeeded\", \"failed\"})\n--\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-118-\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-119-\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-120-@dataclass(frozen=True)\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py:121:class WriteBoundaries:\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-122-    allowed_paths: tuple[str, ...]\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-123-    denied_paths: tuple[str, ...]\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-124-\n--\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-138-        return {\"allowed_paths\": list(self.allowed_paths), \"denied_paths\": list(self.denied_paths)}\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-139-\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-140-    @classmethod\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py:141:    def from_dict(cls, value: Mapping[str, Any]) -> \"WriteBoundaries\":\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-142-        _expect_fields(value, {\"allowed_paths\", \"denied_paths\"}, where=\"write_boundaries\")\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-143-        return cls(value[\"allowed_paths\"], value[\"denied_paths\"])\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-144-\n--\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-195-    prompt: str\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-196-    context_paths: tuple[str, ...]\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-197-    allowed_capabilities: tuple[str, ...]\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py:198:    write_boundaries: WriteBoundaries\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-199-    output_schema: Mapping[str, Any]\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-200-    model_capability_class: str\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-201-    budgets: Budgets\n--\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-226-        if unknown:\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-227-            raise ContractValidationError(f\"unsupported capabilities: {sorted(unknown)}\")\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-228-        object.__setattr__(self, \"allowed_capabilities\", capabilities)\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py:229:        if type(self.write_boundaries) is not WriteBoundaries:\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-230-            raise ContractValidationError(\"write_boundaries has the wrong type\")\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py:231:        has_write = \"repository_write\" in capabilities\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-232-        if has_write and not self.write_boundaries.allowed_paths:\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py:233:            raise ContractValidationError(\"repository_write requires at least one allowed path\")\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py-234-        if not has_write and (self.write_boundaries.allowed_paths or self.write_boundaries.denied_paths):\nPipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py:235:            raise ContractValidationError(\"write paths require repository_write\")\nPipe