{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"jq -r '[.agent,.result.overall_verdict,.result.next_slice.title,.result.alternative_architecture.description]|@tsv' Pipeline/ArchitectureReview/outputs/codex/runs/20260823T102213Z-35a76864/reviews/*.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"jq -r '[.agent,.result.overall_verdict,.result.next_slice.title,.result.alternative_architecture.description]|@tsv' Pipeline/ArchitectureReview/outputs/codex/runs/20260823T102213Z-35a76864/reviews/*.json\"","aggregated_output":"Adversarial QA and Failure-Mode Reviewer\tpartially_unsound\tOne-task delivery lane: NSC-005 mana reset and denied-cast feedback\tReplace the graph-first program with a delivery-first thin control plane. State: separate stable-ID design requirements from repository facts and pipeline policy; keep task contracts only for the near-term frontier. Planning: a human selects priority, then a scoped impact check creates or revises one contract. Execution: one writable agent in one disposable branch/worktree, using the whole small GDD plus targeted files. Validation: typed gates invoke deterministic Git/Unity checks, a fresh semantic diff review, and required human Play Mode checks. Recovery: append-only attempt records, checkpoint commits, bounded retries, no-op detection, and resumable branches. Integration: human merge, post-merge validation on the exact commit, then a delivery receipt referencing requirement revisions and automatically discovered dependency surfaces.\nAutonomous-Agent Architect\tpartially_unsound\tFeature-first delivery kernel: mouse-directed movement\tReorganize around one feature-delivery transaction rather than a hierarchy of global planning and evidence systems. State: keep product canon/design decisions separate from pipeline policy and repository inventory; use a small approved feature contract, Git commit/tree, and one append-only attempt journal as the principal records. Planning: a human selects priority, then one bounded planning/impact pass identifies relevant requirements, files, tests, and unresolved decisions just in time. Execution: a restartable state machine moves one worktree through selected → implementing → validating → human review → merged/blocked, using one write-capable coding worker initially. Validation: task-specific Git scope checks, Unity compilation/tests, clean-tree verification, fresh semantic review when useful, and explicit human Play Mode criteria produce one gate report attached to the candidate commit. Recovery: preserve the worktree, commit, failed gate results, retry count, and next action; measure progress by resolved gates and relevant diffs, not merely any changed file. GDD change: create a reviewed change event mapping stable requirement IDs to affected contracts, tests, and implementation surfaces; replan or revalidate only those affected. Unity: use an actual Editor/host runner, in-memory or temporary test assets, committed-scene conformance checks, meta preservation, and mandatory human visual/feel review. Reconciliation becomes an occasional audit/migration tool; RAG remains optional navigation; GER becomes the bounded retry policy inside the delivery state machine; provider adapters remain replaceable plumbing.\nGame Producer and Throughput Reviewer\tpartially_unsound\tActual game production: deliver NSC-005 end to end\tReorganize around a thin, change-driven delivery controller. State: keep approved GDD requirements and immutable task-contract revisions in Git; keep one operational lifecycle ledger for planned/running/validating/blocked/review/done; treat the merge commit plus evidence manifest as delivery truth. Planning: human-prioritize one vertical slice and link it to stable requirement IDs; GDD diffs impact only linked work. Execution: one scoped writable coding worker on a branch, with checkpoint commits. Validation: deterministic Git checks, a real Windows Unity compile/EditMode/PlayMode/build adapter, one semantic diff review, and explicit human visual/feel gates. Recovery: reconcile attempt IDs against branches, commits, Unity artifacts, and merges so retries are idempotent. Unity integration: maintain one validated canonical scene registry and enforce project-lock/import-cache policy. Keep the existing GDDRAG, clean Unity runner, bounded runtime, and evidence concepts; demote global reconciliation to occasional audits.\nPragmatic Game Technical Director\tpartially_unsound\tPlayable mouse movement and door-approach delivery lane\tReplace the milestone stack with a thin delivery-first loop. State: keep the GDD, Git main, and small versioned contracts only for active/near-term slices; derive operational status from persisted run state, Git/PR state, and validation manifests. Planning: a human selects the next vertical slice and approves its behavior; an LLM produces a bounded contract plus GDD-section impact map. Execution: a local driver creates one branch/worktree and invokes one write-capable worker, followed by a fresh reviewer. Validation: run deterministic checks and Unity compile/EditMode/PlayMode tests through the clean runner, then require human checks for feel and visuals. Recovery: persist a small state machine—planned, implementing, validating, needs-repair, needs-human, merged—with commits, evidence paths, and bounded retry counts. GDD changes: map changed sections or stable requirement IDs only to affected contracts, classifying them as unaffected, contract-review, revalidation, or rework; never globally rebuild the backlog by default. Unity integration: the Windows Unity host owns engine execution, outputs XML/logs outside the repository, checks tree cleanliness, and distinguishes in-memory builders from committed scene/prefab conformance.\nLLM Reliability Engineer\tpartially_unsound\tNSC-003A mouse movement vertical slice through a thin delivery lane\tUse a thin feature-delivery kernel. State: separate stable product requirements from engineering policy and generated repository inventory; bind feature contracts only to relevant requirement IDs. Planning: select and clarify one near-term vertical slice, with scoped impact analysis for later canon changes instead of global reconciliation. Execution: one write-capable agent in an isolated branch/worktree, using externally enforced file and command permissions. Validation: Git/scope checks, clean Unity Edit/Play Mode tests, one fresh semantic diff review, then targeted human experiential review. Recovery: preserve the branch and attempt journal, feed specific failure evidence into at most two repairs, then escalate. Unity integration: explicitly distinguish in-memory builders from committed scenes/prefabs and require non-mutating validation. Add deterministic scheduling only after several successful deliveries.\nUnity Production Engineer\tpartially_unsound\tNSC-003A — End-to-End Mouse Movement Delivery Lane\tReorganize around a thin, single-feature delivery ledger. State: stable requirement IDs/revisions plus Git, small near-frontier contracts, append-only attempt journals, and delivery receipts. Planning: human selects one feature; a planner and Unity scanner validate one contract and its actual paths/GUIDs. Execution: one writable provider in an isolated worktree. Validation: deterministic diff/scope checks, Unity compile, EditMode/PlayMode tests, exact committed-scene inspection, semantic review, and human playtesting. Recovery: preserve branch commits and stage journals, resume from the failed stage, and circuit-break after bounded repairs. Unity integration: serialize only through approved editor/builder operations, retain `.meta` identity, run one host Unity job at a time, and compare canonical asset bytes before/after tests.\nWorkflow and Distributed-Systems Architect\tpartially_unsound\tRepair authority drift, then ship NSC-005 through a no-new-platform delivery lane\tReplace the milestone-platform plan with a thin vertical-slice delivery coordinator. State: stable requirement IDs/revisions in the GDD, small Git-versioned task contracts, one local SQLite/event journal for transient execution, Git commits as implementation truth, immutable external validation manifests, and GitHub as a rebuildable projection only. Planning: keep a rolling three-to-five-item frontier chosen by the human; decompose only the selected slice. Execution: one write-capable agent in one branch/worktree. Validation: deterministic Git checks, Windows Unity compile/EditMode/PlayMode runs, one semantic diff review, then human experiential review. Recovery: explicit compare-and-set transitions with idempotency keys—planned, claimed, workspace_ready, implemented, validating, needs_human, merge_ready, merged, verified—and reconciliation against actual Git refs/PR state after restart. GDD changes: diff stable requirement revisions and invalidate only referencing tasks/evidence plus affected dependents. Unity integration: one Windows host adapter owns the Editor lock, exact Unity version, result XML/log collection, repository-mutation checks, and scene/prefab inspection handoff.\nYAGNI and Complexity Critic\tpartially_unsound\tGameplay-first mouse movement delivery experiment\tReplace the subsystem roadmap with a thin gameplay-delivery lane. State consists of: the human-approved GDD/decision records, small task contracts, integrated main, one append-only attempt/receipt per delivery, and explicit human approvals. Planning is human-prioritized and just-in-time; a single coding worker plans and implements one bounded slice in an isolated worktree. Validation combines scope/diff checks, the existing clean Unity runner, task-specific Edit/Play Mode tests, one fresh semantic review, and a human game-feel/visual gate. Failures return one feedback bundle through at most two repairs. Recovery uses the worktree, checkpoint commits, and a small attempt manifest. After human merge, a receipt binds the integrated commit, relevant canon excerpts, contract revision, test XML, and approval. Readiness derives from merged receipts. GDD edits trigger scoped diff review of referenced sections, not global reconciliation or global invalidation.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_79","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"better_next_step_if_any\":\"I’ve completed the evidence pass. The strongest counter-case is not that delivery-first is wrong; it is that the synthesis has repackaged platform-first work inside the “minimum” lane and selected a feature whose success cannot discriminate that architecture from a simple manual coding workflow. I’m doing the final clean-tree check and then will return a concrete verdict with revision conditions.\",\"failure_if_followed\":[\"The team may spend the first slice building orchestration and requirements infrastructure while believing it has stopped platform-first development.\",\"A green debug-mana slice may be overclaimed as evidence that autonomous Unity integration works.\"],\"final_assessment\":\"synthesis_needs_revision\",\"hidden_assumptions\":[\"That the new lane’s primitives are cheaper than the feature they are meant to deliver.\",\"That NSC-005 provides representative evidence of Unity delivery.\"],\"ignored_minority_arguments\":[\"The no-new-platform/YAGNI position: record the first real lifecycle manually and implement coordinator code only for a failure actually observed.\",\"The workflow-authority position: human approval must be authenticated and lifecycle transitions need explicit idempotency/compare-and-set semantics.\"],\"reason\":\"The diagnosis is well supported, but the recommended cure is not yet minimal, discriminating, or authority-complete.\",\"strongest_counter_case\":\"Use Git/worktree plus the existing clean Unity runner as a human-operated baseline, with a named integration branch and a short receipt; do not add stable requirement IDs, a driver, or resumability code before observed need. Treat NSC-005 as a baseline at most, then validate the architecture on an approved NSC-003A movement slice that exercises real input, scene, and Unity integration.\",\"synthesis_weaknesses\":[\"Selective GDD invalidation is proposed before impact completeness is proven.\",\"The write-capability enforcement boundary is unspecified.\",\"The first-slice success criteria include an unexercisable human reset check and arbitrary throughput thresholds.\"],\"what_would_change_my_mind\":[]}"}}
